1
00:00:00,031 --> 00:00:05,980
Two rounds of diving to come and this is how it stands as we head into the final stages of this competition.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:28,114
Tonya Couch leads still for Great Britain with a really good score but it's this second page where all the action is because the top 12 of 20 go through to the final in this women's 10 meter platform and at the moment it's Green Agadama of Lithuania that has dived herself into a qualification zone.

3
00:00:29,242 --> 00:00:31,263
Germany's Christina Ahsen.

4
00:00:33,125 --> 00:00:36,729
Great start, then a little wobble, then a brilliant comeback.

5
00:00:37,831 --> 00:00:41,554
So the 16-year-old looking good for a place in the final.

6
00:00:41,594 --> 00:00:43,296
Forward three and a half then for round four.

7
00:00:47,801 --> 00:00:54,387
That's a lot of rotation in the pike position and knew it, she had to leave this dive spinning a bit longer than she wanted and ran out of room.

8
00:00:54,689 --> 00:01:06,186
Yeah, now classic mistake, jumps forward, but here she pulls in and suddenly it picks up the rotation and she was surprised by it and came out too late.

9
00:01:06,206 --> 00:01:07,287
49.50.

10
00:01:09,591 --> 00:01:16,281
If you've ever sat in one of those rotating office chairs, put your arms and legs out and rotated, you'll go around quite slowly.

11
00:01:16,563 --> 00:01:21,028
And while you're doing that, then pull your arms and legs in fast and watch your increased rotation.

12
00:01:21,329 --> 00:01:23,412
And that's basically the physics that are working here.

13
00:01:24,727 --> 00:01:27,370
By the way, don't hurt yourself while you're doing it.

14
00:01:30,213 --> 00:01:33,496
Pichikova needs a recovery dive here.

15
00:01:33,537 --> 00:01:36,161
Arm stand forward, two somersaults, single twist.

16
00:01:39,844 --> 00:01:40,626
Lovely arm stand.

17
00:01:44,090 --> 00:01:46,712
Oh, that's a classy dive from start to finish.

18
00:01:46,953 --> 00:01:48,454
Yeah, I like the start there.

19
00:01:48,534 --> 00:01:52,540
Hips forward, flick off, bend the twist, and then the line up.

20
00:01:54,004 --> 00:02:02,117
She bends her arms, that's the right way to go, just a little bit low though, with the head going past the board, but it's the entry that's important.

21
00:02:03,379 --> 00:02:07,486
And into the 60s, Pechikova should climb a couple of places with that one.

22
00:02:13,676 --> 00:02:14,899
Tianga Vila-Kromos then.

23
00:02:14,938 --> 00:02:18,324
Talked about this twister for her.

24
00:02:19,334 --> 00:02:20,715
during the course of the competition.

25
00:02:20,895 --> 00:02:26,001
Is this the dive that is going to be a problem because she has a lot of heavy black tape around her neck?

26
00:02:28,263 --> 00:02:29,443
This will put the head under pressure.

27
00:02:31,086 --> 00:02:32,667
Oh, it's kept the head in place.

28
00:02:32,766 --> 00:02:33,527
Beautifully done.

29
00:02:33,867 --> 00:02:35,050
Yeah, no wobble at all.

30
00:02:37,171 --> 00:02:38,393
Ah, it's a brilliant twist.

31
00:02:38,413 --> 00:02:39,373
That's the way to do it.

32
00:02:39,394 --> 00:02:41,575
A slight over-twist going through the water.

33
00:02:42,257 --> 00:02:45,419
I think because the dive is so pretty, they're not going to mark too many points off.

34
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:47,502
Might just keep it under 60.

35
00:02:50,097 --> 00:02:50,477
57-40.

36
00:02:50,638 --> 00:02:57,445
Villa-Cormos, I think she's going to be OK with that score.

37
00:02:57,466 --> 00:03:01,150
I think they should maintain her qualification position with one round to go.

38
00:03:02,170 --> 00:03:06,736
No problem so far, though, in terms of qualification for Great Britain's Tonya Couch.

39
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:17,909
First position for the last couple of rounds, back two and a half somersaults, one and a half twists in the pike position then for Tonya in round four at 3.2.

40
00:03:23,223 --> 00:03:28,433
will most definitely be a medal contender come this evening because she is going to be in the final.

41
00:03:28,454 --> 00:03:30,277
Yeah, very strong take off.

42
00:03:30,298 --> 00:03:33,223
Just a little loose with the legs going through the water.

43
00:03:34,766 --> 00:03:35,348
Good twist.

44
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:38,275
Reasonably strong pull in on the bike.

45
00:03:39,137 --> 00:03:40,359
Not fully locked out on the end.

46
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:42,143
It doesn't matter though.

47
00:03:42,527 --> 00:03:43,508
The crowd are loving this.

48
00:03:44,270 --> 00:03:49,556
All the school children in for this afternoon's session, enjoying the fact that Couch keeps getting the scores.

49
00:03:50,197 --> 00:03:55,002
They keep putting number one beside her name, and that's what the fans are enjoying.

50
00:03:57,466 --> 00:04:01,771
Now, Kristina Sieszka doesn't look like she's enjoyed her competition, I'm afraid.

51
00:04:01,831 --> 00:04:06,377
The young Belarus diver back three and a half somersaults in the tuck position.

52
00:04:06,837 --> 00:04:08,038
This is a big dive.

53
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:11,943
This is joint most difficult dive in the competition.

54
00:04:12,969 --> 00:04:18,016
And the way she's been diving, Chris, well, you don't hold out much hope, really.

55
00:04:18,036 --> 00:04:21,401
Yeah, Georgia Ward did the back three and a half and went short on the entry.

56
00:04:32,877 --> 00:04:35,060
Oh, well, she just about got there.

57
00:04:35,139 --> 00:04:35,540
Well done.

58
00:04:36,601 --> 00:04:38,504
Yeah, and that was a real struggle.

59
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:44,045
The head's in the wrong position, it's spinning slow, and they're very untidy as she kicks out.

60
00:04:47,309 --> 00:04:49,771
And the huge twist going through the water.

61
00:04:51,093 --> 00:04:51,574
44.55.

62
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:55,658
I think the fact that she's safely down, more important.

63
00:04:56,399 --> 00:04:58,420
But Sheska won't be heading to the final.

64
00:05:01,423 --> 00:05:03,665
Sophia Reisinger, if she wants to go,

65
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,523
to a European Championship final here in London.

66
00:05:07,163 --> 00:05:13,069
Then she has to hit this dive and she has to hit her final round dive as well, both at 2.8.

67
00:05:13,589 --> 00:05:15,132
Reverse two and a half.

68
00:05:15,531 --> 00:05:18,495
She's 35 points out of 12th place.

69
00:05:25,322 --> 00:05:29,045
No, and that is probably it, I'm afraid, for Sophia for today.

70
00:05:29,846 --> 00:05:30,867
That's a poor dive.

71
00:05:31,439 --> 00:05:37,487
She jumps forward, she feels slow in the spin so she's overcompensated by staying in the tuck longer.

72
00:05:37,526 --> 00:05:44,295
Also she has a problem spotting on this dive, she doesn't see the water before kicking out.

73
00:05:47,641 --> 00:05:51,786
Fairly passive response at the moment but she will be very disappointed.

74
00:05:53,108 --> 00:05:58,154
Expected to see Sofia in the final but not happening I'm afraid for the 26-year-old Hungarian.

75
00:05:59,333 --> 00:06:04,281
Arm stand back to somersaults with one and a half twists then for Laura Marrano of France.

76
00:06:04,341 --> 00:06:11,110
She finishes with two twisting dives both at 3.2 and she is on her way at the moment to the final.

77
00:06:27,576 --> 00:06:28,276
Good position.

78
00:06:32,492 --> 00:06:34,175
Yeah, good dive from Marinosa.

79
00:06:34,254 --> 00:06:34,815
That'll be fine.

80
00:06:35,838 --> 00:06:37,600
Yeah, she gets to jump off the platform.

81
00:06:39,122 --> 00:06:40,423
Yeah, good jump.

82
00:06:40,444 --> 00:06:42,968
Just a little anxiety and scrappy with the feet, though.

83
00:06:44,009 --> 00:06:48,514
They're the feet apart, and then they come apart again here before she lines up.

84
00:06:49,136 --> 00:06:50,879
She loses about five or six points for that.

85
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:56,026
57.60, though, is going to be absolutely fine for Laura.

86
00:06:56,245 --> 00:07:01,132
France still going along well with both divers.

87
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:06,127
16th place for Ellen Eck.

88
00:07:06,187 --> 00:07:12,817
If she wanted a place in the top 12 today she knew that every single dive had to be as good as she could make it.

89
00:07:12,877 --> 00:07:18,244
She's been just back off her best so these last two rounds are vital.

90
00:07:18,283 --> 00:07:21,249
She might need another diver to miss as well if she's going to qualify.

91
00:07:23,471 --> 00:07:25,855
She's 33 points out of top 12.

92
00:07:28,535 --> 00:07:30,137
So close.

93
00:07:30,156 --> 00:07:33,120
She'll be disappointed with the entry because it was all going well.

94
00:07:34,543 --> 00:07:36,024
Just everything's too slow though.

95
00:07:37,446 --> 00:07:39,809
Finished about three and a half metres off the water.

96
00:07:39,829 --> 00:07:41,670
Need to finish a lot higher than that.

97
00:07:42,192 --> 00:07:43,112
Good pike position.

98
00:07:43,853 --> 00:07:48,860
The hands just get caught in front of the ears and so the water splashed off the top of their head.

99
00:07:49,961 --> 00:07:52,805
Just 52.20 then for Ellen.

100
00:07:54,687 --> 00:07:56,550
Qualification remains in doubt.

101
00:07:59,077 --> 00:07:59,920
That's a nice look.

102
00:08:02,004 --> 00:08:11,240
That's been around about the ninth position for the whole of the competition, the 20-year-old Ukraine diver, so he's looking at a place in the final.

103
00:08:11,261 --> 00:08:17,273
Back two and a half somersaults in the pike position then at 2.9, but there's no room for error here for Hanna.

104
00:08:29,572 --> 00:08:31,394
Yeah, it's a good dive under pressure.

105
00:08:31,913 --> 00:08:35,037
Wasn't sure she was going to make that with that leave of the platform.

106
00:08:35,898 --> 00:08:38,500
Yeah, when she jumped, she didn't extend her legs.

107
00:08:38,539 --> 00:08:39,541
Her legs are bent.

108
00:08:41,822 --> 00:08:43,924
But the pike here on the second part of the dive was good.

109
00:08:44,385 --> 00:08:45,826
And then she disappears.

110
00:08:46,668 --> 00:08:48,129
And the feet, a lot better as well.

111
00:08:48,168 --> 00:08:49,110
Nicely pointed.

112
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:52,072
So judges like that, 56.55.

113
00:08:52,432 --> 00:08:57,957
And that should protect Krasnoshlyk's place at the moment.

114
00:08:58,798 --> 00:09:04,010
Georgia Ward had one little blip in her program.

115
00:09:07,418 --> 00:09:13,433
Ever popular with the crowd, the British divers, but she's recovered nicely from her blip.

116
00:09:14,636 --> 00:09:16,520
Round four then, forward three and a half.

117
00:09:21,682 --> 00:09:24,485
Oh, and that one's whipped over at the end as well.

118
00:09:24,826 --> 00:09:26,467
And we'll see what the judges do with this.

119
00:09:27,168 --> 00:09:28,091
Oh, what a takeoff.

120
00:09:28,191 --> 00:09:28,932
It was brilliant.

121
00:09:28,971 --> 00:09:30,474
She finishes so high.

122
00:09:30,494 --> 00:09:32,436
There's the double coming around.

123
00:09:32,475 --> 00:09:33,096
One more.

124
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,802
I don't think she was used to such a great takeoff.

125
00:09:38,423 --> 00:09:39,605
That was superb.

126
00:09:39,985 --> 00:09:42,549
But unfortunately, entry's so important.

127
00:09:43,071 --> 00:09:43,971
46.50.

128
00:09:45,013 --> 00:09:50,220
Georgia Ward is going to have to find her best in the last round if she wants to qualify for this evening's final.

129
00:09:50,841 --> 00:09:58,875
That'd be such a shame if she missed out because she is clearly a talent and could definitely put pressure on for the medals.

130
00:09:58,894 --> 00:10:12,657
15th position at the moment for Celine Van Doorn, had done some great work to get into the top 12, rose as high as 11 and then a miss in the last round.

131
00:10:13,778 --> 00:10:17,625
So this arm stand back to somersaults with one and a half twists has got to be good.

132
00:10:21,065 --> 00:10:25,068
Little too quick out of that one and a little too splashy going through the water.

133
00:10:25,188 --> 00:10:27,410
I'm not sure this will improve her situation.

134
00:10:28,511 --> 00:10:31,193
Very lucky on the end here.

135
00:10:31,214 --> 00:10:33,596
Gets the push but late into the twist.

136
00:10:35,357 --> 00:10:39,481
Just gets the hands to the water but not fully locked out.

137
00:10:40,081 --> 00:10:41,864
Oh, they've liked it.

138
00:10:41,884 --> 00:10:43,985
She'll take that any day of the week.

139
00:10:44,005 --> 00:10:44,567
62.40.

140
00:10:45,366 --> 00:10:48,269
She was expecting to turn around and see a mid-50 score there.

141
00:10:48,807 --> 00:10:51,169
But Salim Van Doorn is still in business.

142
00:10:53,831 --> 00:10:57,696
Anvilder Tuiksen in last place at the moment.

143
00:10:59,457 --> 00:11:02,380
Some personal goals will have been set for today's performance.

144
00:11:02,782 --> 00:11:05,063
It'll be all about the score.

145
00:11:07,407 --> 00:11:09,269
Two dives left then to prove herself.

146
00:11:12,491 --> 00:11:13,312
Inward two and a half.

147
00:11:17,106 --> 00:11:19,509
And one of her better dives today.

148
00:11:20,830 --> 00:11:23,173
Yeah, this will be the highest scoring dive.

149
00:11:23,232 --> 00:11:29,379
She hasn't got above 13 on the first four dives, three dives.

150
00:11:29,999 --> 00:11:34,984
Pulling in hard, but then breaking position, feet going flat before lining up.

151
00:11:35,845 --> 00:11:37,426
Ooh.

152
00:11:37,446 --> 00:11:37,986
42 marks.

153
00:11:38,006 --> 00:11:38,386
42.

154
00:11:38,427 --> 00:11:40,729
There we go.

155
00:11:40,749 --> 00:11:46,995
So took some of the rather solemn look back to the scoreboard as we go back

156
00:11:47,211 --> 00:11:50,054
to the top of our leaderboard with Maria Cujo.

157
00:11:51,115 --> 00:11:54,779
Back two and a half somersaults in the pike position then for the German.

158
00:11:57,283 --> 00:12:00,287
A little bit like Bakke today, she's kind of slid under the radar.

159
00:12:01,567 --> 00:12:03,429
Just gone about her business and has been solid.

160
00:12:06,033 --> 00:12:10,037
And okay, not her best, but that's still heading towards qualification.

161
00:12:10,317 --> 00:12:13,380
Yeah, it's been very consistent.

162
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:16,965
First dive sixth place, then in second, then third.

163
00:12:18,716 --> 00:12:21,720
This will keep her up in the top five or six.

164
00:12:23,761 --> 00:12:24,543
Yeah, no problems.

165
00:12:24,602 --> 00:12:25,383
56.55.

166
00:12:25,604 --> 00:12:33,751
Quick check with the coach about their view on that particular dive, but that's fine.

167
00:12:34,793 --> 00:12:37,215
Liliya Prokopchuk.

168
00:12:37,235 --> 00:12:44,241
With the big names, you're never far away from a dive that just establishes exactly where they are in the pecking order.

169
00:12:44,282 --> 00:12:46,563
And in the last round, Prokopchuk

170
00:12:46,966 --> 00:12:49,232
sent out a little message to the rest of the field.

171
00:12:50,316 --> 00:12:52,461
If you want gold, it's me you've got to beat.

172
00:12:53,706 --> 00:12:55,029
Great diving to recover.

173
00:12:55,410 --> 00:13:00,145
Arm stand back, three somersaults in the tuck position at 3.3.

174
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:01,649
Big dive.

175
00:13:04,701 --> 00:13:07,725
And a big score coming, a really big score coming.

176
00:13:08,106 --> 00:13:11,972
I think she's about 75, 76 points behind Tonya Couch.

177
00:13:12,734 --> 00:13:16,479
And this 3-3 is going to definitely be in the 70s.

178
00:13:17,561 --> 00:13:19,683
Strong kick out, great reach back.

179
00:13:22,727 --> 00:13:24,630
Oh, look at that, 75-90.

180
00:13:25,251 --> 00:13:29,577
And Prokopchuk reclaims the lead from Tonya Couch.

181
00:13:35,886 --> 00:13:53,748
At the top of the leaderboard there's just 0.15 in it between Prokopchuk and Couch and the likes of Cuiar, Marino and Batki all through.

182
00:13:54,107 --> 00:13:56,831
But it's this part of the leaderboard that we're interested in.

183
00:13:56,851 --> 00:13:58,833
Angadama hangs on to 12th position.

184
00:13:58,913 --> 00:14:02,197
Georgia Ward has improved her placing to 13th.

185
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:07,376
for Great Britain, but this final round of diving is going to be very tense indeed.

186
00:14:13,101 --> 00:14:16,404
Horrendously difficult competition to qualify through to the final.

187
00:14:16,645 --> 00:14:21,870
20 divers, 12 places available off the women's 10 metre platform for this evening's final.

188
00:14:21,950 --> 00:14:30,238
Naomi Backke next onto the board should be going there for Italy without any dramas, but there's a lot of drama around position 12 at the moment.

189
00:14:31,058 --> 00:14:32,639
Italy then for a place in the final.

190
00:14:36,687 --> 00:14:42,212
And the 28-year-old, she won't be pleased with that dive, but she'll be appearing tonight to compete for medals.

191
00:14:42,613 --> 00:14:48,779
Yeah, jumps away from the platform, cuts off the height, and another diver finishing low to the water.

192
00:14:48,799 --> 00:14:52,823
But she was in fifth, and she will dive better in the final.

193
00:14:53,124 --> 00:14:55,427
Former European champion back in 2011.

194
00:14:56,548 --> 00:14:58,009
Just licking a little bit off at the moment.

195
00:14:58,028 --> 00:14:59,191
284, though.

196
00:14:59,791 --> 00:15:01,373
That's a comfortable qualification.

197
00:15:02,553 --> 00:15:04,416
And she and Mam Ibole

198
00:15:05,019 --> 00:15:11,986
She'll be going away to have a chat about how they put that dive list together for this evening's final.

199
00:15:12,006 --> 00:15:16,511
Back to the other end of the leaderboard and Isabelle Svantesen of Sweden.

200
00:15:16,751 --> 00:15:21,557
This is about signing off in style and coming away with a positive dive.

201
00:15:22,158 --> 00:15:23,538
She won't be going to the final.

202
00:15:26,701 --> 00:15:32,427
But she has benefited from the experience and again another diver going a long, long way down the pool and away from the platform.

203
00:15:33,370 --> 00:15:34,851
Yeah, just it's the technique.

204
00:15:34,871 --> 00:15:40,238
If you haven't got the right timing on the jump, the momentum of the run down the board just drags you forward.

205
00:15:41,899 --> 00:15:43,421
Highest score so far is 46.

206
00:15:43,741 --> 00:15:46,225
There we go.

207
00:15:46,644 --> 00:15:48,047
An improvement and a positive.

208
00:15:48,067 --> 00:15:57,157
47.85, but still under the 200 mark across five rounds of diving.

209
00:15:57,177 --> 00:15:59,500
Christina Bassen shouldn't be a problem for her.

210
00:15:59,539 --> 00:16:01,621
Sixth position at the moment.

211
00:16:02,732 --> 00:16:04,735
finishes with this back twister at 3.2.

212
00:16:06,879 --> 00:16:10,563
And on occasion, the German has looked really good.

213
00:16:16,913 --> 00:16:21,399
And she will be trying to dive like that all the way through the final this evening.

214
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:23,623
Yeah, it's a good strong finish.

215
00:16:24,182 --> 00:16:25,365
Beautiful twist.

216
00:16:26,509 --> 00:16:28,152
And she knows the end sheet again.

217
00:16:28,451 --> 00:16:29,633
She will be pleased with this.

218
00:16:29,653 --> 00:16:34,979
She finished 15th last year, had a terrible competition, and didn't make the final.

219
00:16:35,879 --> 00:16:38,822
First diver over 300 is Kristina Vassin.

220
00:16:39,283 --> 00:16:40,785
Another 70 score for her.

221
00:16:42,246 --> 00:16:44,328
And the smile confirms a place in the final.

222
00:16:45,770 --> 00:16:48,052
So Germany should qualify two through.

223
00:16:49,274 --> 00:16:54,120
Russia still in doubt as to whether they can qualify both their divers.

224
00:16:55,585 --> 00:16:56,505
Is there hope now?

225
00:16:56,525 --> 00:16:59,490
Seventh position after four rounds.

226
00:16:59,650 --> 00:17:02,836
Final dive back two and a half somersaults with one and a half twists.

227
00:17:09,547 --> 00:17:12,090
And that will be Ekaterina through to the final again.

228
00:17:12,230 --> 00:17:14,775
Not her best by any means, but safe enough.

229
00:17:15,717 --> 00:17:30,217
same thing bends the knees and the hips go back so it's jumping backwards into the twister rather than up and it makes it hard to pull into the pike after one and a half twists.

230
00:17:30,237 --> 00:17:31,077
286.35.

231
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:33,280
She's safe.

