This is back to square one.

450
00:35:26,436 --> 00:35:27,721
Marillot then for France.

451
00:35:27,800 --> 00:35:30,250
Inward three and a half in the tuck position.

452
00:35:42,143 --> 00:35:43,565
Oh, it's a miss.

453
00:35:44,005 --> 00:35:46,811
And this is what the contest could come down to tonight, Chris.

454
00:35:47,231 --> 00:35:49,554
If you do miss, it's by how much you miss.

455
00:35:50,217 --> 00:35:51,518
Yeah, and that was disastrous.

456
00:35:51,539 --> 00:35:54,483
She went 72 points in the prelims.

457
00:35:54,764 --> 00:35:57,829
There, though, she fell out of it out too late.

458
00:35:57,849 --> 00:36:01,815
Little bit close with her hair coming around on the first somersault.

459
00:36:01,835 --> 00:36:02,777
There's that miss there.

460
00:36:02,797 --> 00:36:05,041
Doesn't pick up the water on the triple.

461
00:36:05,322 --> 00:36:08,387
You need to be able to spot the water, come out quick.

462
00:36:10,780 --> 00:36:12,362
Silver medal last year.

463
00:36:13,083 --> 00:36:16,347
Well, this was, as Chris said, 72 in the prelims.

464
00:36:16,367 --> 00:36:17,268
This will be closer to 27.

465
00:36:17,289 --> 00:36:22,036
It's certainly not going to make it into the 50s.

466
00:36:23,518 --> 00:36:26,481
Remains to be seen if she can make it into the 40s.

467
00:36:27,324 --> 00:36:27,724
She can.

468
00:36:27,744 --> 00:36:28,865
49.60.

469
00:36:28,965 --> 00:36:36,737
So Marrano gets off to a poor start and the 2015 silver medalist in this event under pressure already.

470
00:36:38,050 --> 00:36:41,516
Now, what a refreshing change this young lady was earlier today.

471
00:36:41,536 --> 00:36:55,586
17-year-old Genevieve Green Anjarami from Lithuania, but actually left Lithuania when she was two years of age and has done all of her diving in the USA, trains alongside World Championship Synchro finalist Kasady Kuk.

472
00:36:59,092 --> 00:37:02,376
And a horrible inward two and a half to start, I'm afraid.

473
00:37:02,396 --> 00:37:03,617
And you heard the crowd groan.

474
00:37:03,677 --> 00:37:04,838
This has gone badly wrong.

475
00:37:05,019 --> 00:37:07,342
Yeah, it's right on the start.

476
00:37:07,402 --> 00:37:09,063
She slips right here.

477
00:37:09,625 --> 00:37:14,110
Oh, she is so lucky that that didn't go badly, badly wrong for her.

478
00:37:15,271 --> 00:37:18,994
Yeah, she slips and you just, there was nothing to push against.

479
00:37:21,757 --> 00:37:25,202
She was actually lucky that her feet didn't hit on that first somersault as well.

480
00:37:26,177 --> 00:37:27,701
That would have stopped her completely there.

481
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:28,543
She's smiling.

482
00:37:28,782 --> 00:37:29,945
Oh, she's unbelievable.

483
00:37:29,965 --> 00:37:30,806
They're tough, aren't they?

484
00:37:30,907 --> 00:37:32,230
Yeah, still smiling away.

485
00:37:32,269 --> 00:37:38,922
Whole competition to go, but has to accept a sub-20 mark, I'm afraid, for that opener.

486
00:37:38,983 --> 00:37:42,730
So Anjan Ami, having made the final, big day for her.

487
00:37:42,769 --> 00:37:44,534
That was a huge result.

488
00:37:44,554 --> 00:37:48,320
Unfortunately, hasn't got the start she wanted in the final itself.

489
00:37:51,541 --> 00:37:56,306
Next up from the Netherlands, Celine van Doen, 23 years of age now, starts with a back twister.

490
00:37:56,326 --> 00:38:00,710
So back two and a half somersaults with one and a half twists in the pike position.

491
00:38:03,972 --> 00:38:14,342
Well, you just heard in the background the announcer here in the stadium just letting everybody know that there is an input issue with the scoring pads.

492
00:38:14,382 --> 00:38:19,829
We've had the odd electronic gremlin during the course of this week, Chris, but it's to be expected.

493
00:38:19,849 --> 00:38:21,210
It's a very complex system.

494
00:38:21,697 --> 00:38:48,362
It is and what happens though if the pads don't work and it looks like it's going to delay the competition then they go to flip cards the old system back to the good old days yes and i think that's when color telly was just being invented as well it's always a bit of fun to see that let's hope that they do manage to fix the problem quickly because we all enjoy

495
00:38:48,815 --> 00:38:56,344
Seeing the graphics come up, the split of all the marks from all the judges, that's tremendously helpful from everyone's point of view.

496
00:38:57,065 --> 00:39:00,911
It's really hard to use the flip cards nowadays because they blinker the judges.

497
00:39:01,030 --> 00:39:06,137
So in between each of the judges there is a screen and you can't look across.

498
00:39:06,197 --> 00:39:12,487
That also means that the judges closest to the recorder's table won't be able to see anything that the judges put up.

499
00:39:12,507 --> 00:39:18,534
And there's three of them over there and there's four on the far side where the three meter springboards are.

500
00:39:19,139 --> 00:39:23,686
Well, it's thrown the judging committee and the panel into a bit of turmoil.

501
00:39:24,226 --> 00:39:31,876
And they're all now holding up the cards on the main table, holding up the cards for the judges to say, look, this is what we've got to go to.

502
00:39:31,896 --> 00:39:33,739
We've got to go to the old paper system.

503
00:39:34,840 --> 00:39:37,105
So electronics at the moment look to be out the window.

504
00:39:37,125 --> 00:39:39,829
This is not good for Celine Van Duyn, incidentally.

505
00:39:40,409 --> 00:39:43,594
It's OK if you're not up there on the steps or up there on the board.

506
00:39:44,266 --> 00:39:46,409
You can take a little bit of a pause.

507
00:39:46,449 --> 00:39:49,253
But if you're already up there, then this is a very twitchy moment.

508
00:39:49,293 --> 00:39:55,121
And if you haven't got your competition underway either as well, then this is going to take a little bit of mental toughness to get through this period.

509
00:39:55,603 --> 00:39:56,905
And it's the first round as well.

510
00:39:56,965 --> 00:40:01,632
And the divers don't get settled until the first dive's over when they get wet.

511
00:40:03,574 --> 00:40:07,481
Well, we had already got confirmation of that mark from Anjanami.

512
00:40:07,521 --> 00:40:09,784
There it is again, 19.60.

513
00:40:10,927 --> 00:40:13,210
So unfortunately, no reprieve for her.

514
00:40:13,731 --> 00:40:20,840
She would just be very grateful that nothing else went wrong with that dive, because once that foot slipped away, she could have been in real trouble.

515
00:40:22,501 --> 00:40:25,105
So time at last for Celine Van Doen.

516
00:40:26,106 --> 00:40:28,449
That back twister that I described at 3.2.

517
00:40:29,909 --> 00:40:35,637
She's got three dives that go into the three, so not a bad dive list from the 23-year-old Dutch woman.

518
00:40:44,222 --> 00:40:47,748
And well, considering the weight, that was a pretty good effort.

519
00:40:48,347 --> 00:40:49,289
Yeah, very good effort.

520
00:40:49,309 --> 00:40:51,793
I did think she was going to ride over on the end, but she didn't.

521
00:40:51,833 --> 00:40:53,074
She controlled the entry.

522
00:40:53,594 --> 00:40:54,195
Here's the jump.

523
00:40:54,235 --> 00:40:55,097
That was good.

524
00:40:55,858 --> 00:40:57,701
Only a little bit away from the platform.

525
00:40:59,242 --> 00:40:59,943
One and a half twist.

526
00:41:00,003 --> 00:41:02,947
Now that's the hard bit pulling forwards into the pike.

527
00:41:03,208 --> 00:41:04,429
Just a small wobble there.

528
00:41:04,469 --> 00:41:10,617
The splash has been thrown up because her hand's not flat enough on the water, but technically a good dive.

529
00:41:11,898 --> 00:41:12,639
in the prelims.

530
00:41:12,958 --> 00:41:14,360
She only went 50 points.

531
00:41:14,920 --> 00:41:15,882
This is far better.

532
00:41:16,621 --> 00:41:18,043
Yes, 65-60.

533
00:41:18,324 --> 00:41:20,585
Great opener.

534
00:41:22,708 --> 00:41:24,489
And not the only person that had to wait.

535
00:41:24,630 --> 00:41:30,074
Krasnozhlyuk of Ukraine would have been halfway up the steps waiting to go.

536
00:41:32,016 --> 00:41:34,378
In with two and a half somersaults then for her.

537
00:41:34,438 --> 00:41:41,364
That's a very good synchro record and has done well with Tatsenko in the past.

538
00:41:41,952 --> 00:41:49,340
But on an individual basis, still looking for that first big result, just outside the medals last time around in fifth position.

539
00:41:54,606 --> 00:41:57,190
But she has a little problem with flattening the feet off.

540
00:41:57,210 --> 00:42:00,072
She did it in the prelims as well, but the dive overall is still good.

541
00:42:00,353 --> 00:42:02,496
Yeah, in the prelims she was close.

542
00:42:02,516 --> 00:42:03,336
This isn't close.

543
00:42:03,396 --> 00:42:05,440
She didn't need to flatten her feet.

544
00:42:05,719 --> 00:42:07,202
I think it's more of a habit now.

545
00:42:07,581 --> 00:42:08,983
That was a really good take off.

546
00:42:09,003 --> 00:42:10,525
Just need to keep those toes pointed.

547
00:42:10,865 --> 00:42:11,806
She would have been all right.

548
00:42:13,777 --> 00:42:14,639
Good entry, though.

549
00:42:16,300 --> 00:42:20,623
So there's only maybe 10 centimeters of splash.

550
00:42:21,605 --> 00:42:22,505
It's going to be a good score.

551
00:42:24,086 --> 00:42:24,867
It is a good score.

552
00:42:24,887 --> 00:42:25,347
63.

553
00:42:25,568 --> 00:42:30,753
Coach Olga Ivanenko with a bit of advice.

554
00:42:31,873 --> 00:42:35,836
And listen to this reception from the home crowd for the home athlete.

555
00:42:35,876 --> 00:42:38,458
Georgia Ward diving in her home pool.

556
00:42:38,840 --> 00:42:43,684
This is where she trains, along with Tom Daley and Coach Jane Figueredo.

557
00:42:45,065 --> 00:42:51,311
already has a bronze medal from this European Championships in the team event with Mattie Lee and has a massive dive list.

558
00:42:51,391 --> 00:43:00,900
She starts with the back twister.

559
00:43:00,920 --> 00:43:02,722
It's okay, it's okay.

560
00:43:02,822 --> 00:43:07,387
In terms of degree of difficulty, Chris, she has got a dive list that can rival anyone.

561
00:43:07,887 --> 00:43:11,010
Yes, there's three divers doing back three and a halfs.

562
00:43:11,030 --> 00:43:12,152
George is one of them.

563
00:43:13,702 --> 00:43:15,324
Well, this is better than the prelims.

564
00:43:15,625 --> 00:43:17,286
It went really over in the prelims.

565
00:43:17,306 --> 00:43:19,088
This is just slightly over.

566
00:43:21,853 --> 00:43:23,876
But technically strong.

567
00:43:23,976 --> 00:43:29,304
I wonder if she'll be strong enough eventually to do two and a half twists.

568
00:43:29,344 --> 00:43:30,264
She's a great diver.

569
00:43:30,364 --> 00:43:31,365
She's already proved that.

570
00:43:31,407 --> 00:43:34,630
Showed good resilience this morning to come back from a bad start.

571
00:43:35,072 --> 00:43:36,713
But that's a good start.

572
00:43:36,733 --> 00:43:38,416
Yeah, it's better than the prelims.

573
00:43:38,996 --> 00:43:39,878
64 marks.

574
00:43:39,898 --> 00:43:41,159
Georgia Ward in good shape.

575
00:43:43,822 --> 00:43:53,797
28 years of age alongside Prokopchuk, the most experienced athlete in this field.

576
00:43:58,324 --> 00:44:05,454
She's won this title before, she's not going to win it again with dives like that I'm afraid, a poor forward three and a half somersault opener.

577
00:44:05,494 --> 00:44:10,523
She finished really high, but there's the problem, she's also jumped forward so

578
00:44:10,822 --> 00:44:13,347
Although she's come out late from the pike.

579
00:44:13,367 --> 00:44:15,389
Pike here is good but she is trapping forward.

580
00:44:15,690 --> 00:44:19,614
Hard to stop the rotation and she reaches for the wrong part of the water.

581
00:44:19,675 --> 00:44:24,041
Needed to reach more forward towards the one metre boards on the far side.

582
00:44:26,304 --> 00:44:32,793
Just 45 marks from Batki and in this sort of company you can't afford those errors.

583
00:44:33,034 --> 00:44:37,320
I talked about the fact that there are going to be misses and it's by how much you miss but

584
00:44:37,739 --> 00:44:41,043
45 is probably too much.

585
00:44:41,302 --> 00:44:45,208
She's going to have to rely on other athletes missing dives as well.

586
00:44:45,367 --> 00:44:47,050
So forward three and a half somersaults now.

587
00:44:47,409 --> 00:44:58,222
Same dive from Petrikova of Russia, the 19-year-old coached by her synchro partner's mother, Timoshenina, who saw her daughter miss out in the prelims.

588
00:45:00,846 --> 00:45:02,126
So this is Russia's hope.

589
00:45:02,146 --> 00:45:03,548
It's so-so.

590
00:45:03,608 --> 00:45:06,092
It's not a bad entry, but it was very low.

591
00:45:09,346 --> 00:45:10,728
So strong takeoff.

592
00:45:11,170 --> 00:45:11,931
That was good.

593
00:45:12,393 --> 00:45:13,434
Not traveling forward.

594
00:45:14,097 --> 00:45:17,364
Just lining up in front of the face, going through the water.

595
00:45:17,403 --> 00:45:19,889
So you see, just at the last minute, the feet kick.

596
00:45:20,291 --> 00:45:22,456
She rolls under the water, brings some of it back.

597
00:45:23,677 --> 00:45:25,362
A good jump at the start.

598
00:45:26,826 --> 00:45:27,927
This will be a decent mark.

599
00:45:31,367 --> 00:45:41,101
It's a good opener from Pechikova and she has the lead by just a third of a point from Eli Kalanji of France.

600
00:45:43,342 --> 00:45:48,809
Two Germans to come next and always the same in each rotation of these five rounds.

601
00:45:49,851 --> 00:45:54,657
Maria Corgio already has a gold from the synchro on the 10 meter.

602
00:45:56,697 --> 00:45:58,679
And it's a solid start from her.

603
00:45:58,740 --> 00:46:00,143
Nice entry.

604
00:46:00,704 --> 00:46:01,786
Good forward three and a half.

605
00:46:03,007 --> 00:46:05,753
Yeah, she did something funny with the feet though, going through the water.

606
00:46:08,456 --> 00:46:11,242
Good jump, spinning fast.

607
00:46:11,262 --> 00:46:17,331
Just the feet relaxing right here, which the judges will pick up.

608
00:46:17,452 --> 00:46:20,358
As she rolls, her feet flatten.

609
00:46:20,378 --> 00:46:22,400
It's a shame she'll lose five, six points for that.

610
00:46:24,355 --> 00:46:28,300
But another diver makes it into the 60-point zone.

611
00:46:29,981 --> 00:46:32,965
Good job at the moment in fifth position.

612
00:46:33,025 --> 00:46:39,554
The German pair doing very well today to get through in third and fourth.

613
00:46:39,693 --> 00:46:49,286
But for Christina Vass, and this is uncharted territory, the student from Berlin doesn't have any senior medals yet in the European Championships.

614
00:46:49,327 --> 00:46:50,327
Could today be the day?

615
00:46:50,427 --> 00:46:51,829
In with three and a half somersaults.

616
00:46:51,849 --> 00:46:52,911
This is a big dive.

617
00:46:54,172 --> 00:46:55,994
It was the second highest scoring dive.

618
00:46:57,637 --> 00:46:59,278
No, it's not going to be far away again.

619
00:46:59,338 --> 00:47:01,661
That's a great start from Rassen.

620
00:47:01,681 --> 00:47:02,943
Yeah, 75 points.

621
00:47:03,344 --> 00:47:06,708
I think the one in the prelims, though, the body was just a little tighter.

622
00:47:07,289 --> 00:47:08,369
Springy jump.

623
00:47:10,052 --> 00:47:11,253
Yeah, just there that.

624
00:47:11,333 --> 00:47:11,875
Small mistake.

625
00:47:11,974 --> 00:47:13,096
Everything else, though.

626
00:47:13,115 --> 00:47:13,637
Good tuck.

627
00:47:13,717 --> 00:47:14,657
Squeezing tight.

628
00:47:14,697 --> 00:47:15,559
Spinning fast.

629
00:47:15,659 --> 00:47:16,539
Finishing high.

630
00:47:19,784 --> 00:47:20,284
And it's good.

631
00:47:20,605 --> 00:47:21,405
It's safe as well.

632
00:47:21,626 --> 00:47:23,809
Not too far or too close.

633
00:47:24,463 --> 00:47:24,704
75.

634
00:47:24,724 --> 00:47:26,226
Exactly the same score.

635
00:47:26,306 --> 00:47:28,811
It is the final and the judges have gone with it.

636
00:47:29,090 --> 00:47:35,742
Brilliant diving from Arsene and she opens once again with a 75 pointer to take the lead.

637
00:47:36,603 --> 00:47:38,565
Two divers to come in round one.

638
00:47:38,585 --> 00:47:47,380
Lulia Prokopchuk, the defending champion, looking to add a fifth 10 meter European Championship gold to her CV.

639
00:47:47,699 --> 00:47:52,007
Forward three and a half then in the pike position at 3.0 for Lulia.

640
00:47:56,728 --> 00:47:59,211
It's a much better start than the prelims.

641
00:48:00,413 --> 00:48:02,114
Yeah, the prelims, she only got sixes.

642
00:48:04,257 --> 00:48:05,057
Different pike.

643
00:48:05,398 --> 00:48:09,943
She holds right down the bottom of her legs and has that gap going around.

644
00:48:10,983 --> 00:48:12,686
But she got the tearing rip sound.

645
00:48:13,626 --> 00:48:17,070
There's still a beautiful pike, though.

646
00:48:17,090 --> 00:48:18,452
And look at that little movement.

647
00:48:18,472 --> 00:48:20,193
So she'll get much higher than sixes.

648
00:48:20,213 --> 00:48:26,601
75-2-0 leads for Germany and Christina Assen.

649
00:48:27,103 --> 00:48:32,532
And just underneath that at 72 for a lower degree of difficulty.

650
00:48:32,592 --> 00:48:34,835
That's a fine opener from Prokopchuk.

651
00:48:35,958 --> 00:48:40,184
And once again, the decibel level goes up here in the London Aquatics Centre.

652
00:48:40,204 --> 00:48:47,335
Tonya Couch, the 26-year-old from Plymouth, coached by Andy Banks to open her account in this final.

653
00:48:47,896 --> 00:48:50,599
Same dive that we've just seen from Prokopchuk.

654
00:48:50,619 --> 00:48:52,402
So a little bit of pressure on Couch here.

655
00:48:57,039 --> 00:48:58,782
And that's the way to respond.

656
00:48:59,402 --> 00:49:05,452
Maybe not quite as good on the entry as Prokopchuk, but that will certainly get her off to a great start.

657
00:49:05,532 --> 00:49:07,253
Tonya had a better start, though.

658
00:49:07,293 --> 00:49:09,516
This jumps up in the air, and the pike is better.

659
00:49:09,536 --> 00:49:11,320
The face is across the top of the legs.

660
00:49:11,840 --> 00:49:13,762
Yes, it had a little bit more splash.

661
00:49:14,384 --> 00:49:17,469
But technically, I think this was superior.

662
00:49:17,829 --> 00:49:20,713
Slightly flat feet and then pointed again, coming out.

663
00:49:21,755 --> 00:49:25,679
But the splash, that's what the judges might mark her down for.

664
00:49:26,402 --> 00:49:27,344
Oh, wow.

665
00:49:28,186 --> 00:49:29,849
Well, that was really unfair.

666
00:49:29,929 --> 00:49:31,932
That is a tough call for Tonya Couch.

667
00:49:32,014 --> 00:49:32,954
61-50.

668
00:49:33,235 --> 00:49:33,976
She's not happy.

669
00:49:34,679 --> 00:49:36,983
And that is not the start that she was looking for.

670
00:49:38,125 --> 00:49:39,608
Well, we told you it would be interesting.

671
00:49:39,969 --> 00:49:43,715
It's the youngster, 17-year-old Christina Watson, that leads at the moment.

672
00:49:43,795 --> 00:49:44,918
We'll take the break there.

673
00:49:47,681 --> 00:49:53,630
Round two of the women's 10-meter final on day five here at the European Diving Championships on Eurosport.

674
00:49:53,650 --> 00:49:57,757
Armstand back to somersaults with a half twist for Eli Kalonji of France.

675
00:50:01,382 --> 00:50:02,143
Nicely done.

676
00:50:02,244 --> 00:50:04,567
She started this competition on fire.

677
00:50:05,989 --> 00:50:08,592
Yeah, in fourth place, qualified in 12.

678
00:50:10,766 --> 00:50:13,510
That's a half twist first and then into the pike.

679
00:50:13,992 --> 00:50:16,815
A bit wobbly though with a loose back going through the water.

680
00:50:17,257 --> 00:50:18,057
Good at this point.

681
00:50:19,099 --> 00:50:20,380
Arms lining up in front.

682
00:50:21,141 --> 00:50:22,123
Hardly any splash.

683
00:50:24,827 --> 00:50:28,793
But doesn't really squeeze the ears with the arms and lock the body out.

684
00:50:28,813 --> 00:50:36,505
Well degree of difficulty of just 2.7 is always going to be tough to get yourself into the 60s but solid diving from her.

685
00:50:37,902 --> 00:50:41,646
Now Laura Marino has already made her mistake.

686
00:50:42,809 --> 00:50:44,391
A big miss in round one.

687
00:50:44,490 --> 00:50:45,413
That's out of the way.

688
00:50:46,574 --> 00:50:51,782
She now needs four rounds of world-class diving if she wants a shot at the medal.

689
00:50:52,081 --> 00:50:57,128
Forward three and a half somersaults in the pike position then in round two for Marino.

690
00:51:02,677 --> 00:51:03,538
That's better.

691
00:51:05,239 --> 00:51:07,242
Just a little loose on the entry.

692
00:51:07,983 --> 00:51:09,505
Again, the technique is good.

693
00:51:10,045 --> 00:51:17,034
What we're looking for is upright and then the first part of the somersault to move up and then drop.

694
00:51:17,054 --> 00:51:18,175
So there she gets it.

695
00:51:19,255 --> 00:51:22,119
Pike is near perfect, the face very clushing.

696
00:51:23,641 --> 00:51:24,503
Pulling in hard.

697
00:51:24,722 --> 00:51:27,987
Second and third somersault faster than the first because the pike's tighter.

698
00:51:29,929 --> 00:51:31,670
63 marks for Marinot.

699
00:51:33,672 --> 00:51:34,233
May

700
00:51:34,753 --> 00:51:36,978
Enable her to advance a position or two.

701
00:51:38,782 --> 00:51:46,297
And as Chris Snowd said, 70s is where you need to be this evening if you want to get in amongst the medals and take that gold.

702
00:51:46,858 --> 00:51:52,228
Now, Anjarami, the Lithuanian, a really scary start for her.

703
00:51:52,268 --> 00:51:53,030
She got away with it.

704
00:51:53,632 --> 00:51:56,036
So four, three and a half somersaults in round two.

705
00:51:58,480 --> 00:52:04,746
Oh my goodness me, and it's going from bad to worse, I'm afraid, for the Lithuanian.

706
00:52:04,887 --> 00:52:07,650
That is a poor dive and it's a painful one.

707
00:52:07,670 --> 00:52:10,273
Yeah, so on the inwards she caught it on the face.

708
00:52:10,293 --> 00:52:13,516
Now a whole of her back completely slaps.

709
00:52:15,398 --> 00:52:16,500
So she misses her spot.

710
00:52:16,559 --> 00:52:17,101
This is good.

711
00:52:18,202 --> 00:52:19,362
Lovely tuck position.

712
00:52:20,985 --> 00:52:21,806
And misses it.

713
00:52:21,846 --> 00:52:23,407
Doesn't see the triple.

714
00:52:24,382 --> 00:52:28,730
Divers feel the triple come around, then they look at the water, and then they reach for it.

715
00:52:30,092 --> 00:52:31,434
And she just stayed in the tuck.

716
00:52:32,195 --> 00:52:33,237
Still smiling.

717
00:52:33,637 --> 00:52:34,259
Unbelievable.

718
00:52:35,260 --> 00:52:37,083
And hasn't made it to 30 points yet.

719
00:52:37,664 --> 00:52:41,250
Well, let's just hope, for her sake, that things improve.

720
00:52:44,896 --> 00:52:47,480
Celine van Doornen for the Netherlands.

721
00:52:47,500 --> 00:52:50,063
2.8 for this next round.

722
00:52:50,123 --> 00:52:51,706
Inward two and a half somersaults then.

723
00:52:53,358 --> 00:52:59,347
This is the dive that Kalonjic really nailed first up in this final for France.

724
00:53:00,548 --> 00:53:01,530
What can Celine do?

725
00:53:08,382 --> 00:53:10,125
Well, very graceful through the air.

726
00:53:10,945 --> 00:53:14,351
It looked, if anything, a little easy for her.

727
00:53:14,371 --> 00:53:16,614
That's because she did all the right movements.

728
00:53:17,422 --> 00:53:18,864
The throw was at the right time.

729
00:53:18,923 --> 00:53:21,427
You have to coordinate the throw with the jump.

730
00:53:21,927 --> 00:53:23,289
Pulls it straight away.

731
00:53:23,309 --> 00:53:28,215
So she was into the pike as tight as you can be right at the beginning.

732
00:53:28,255 --> 00:53:31,518
Some of the divers take half a rotation to get in there.

733
00:53:32,039 --> 00:53:34,922
A little splashy on the entry.

734
00:53:34,943 --> 00:53:35,804
58.80.

735
00:53:36,885 --> 00:53:39,849
Keeps Celine Vander and score ticking along nicely.

736
00:53:43,112 --> 00:53:45,335
That's nice lick for Ukraine.

737
00:53:45,990 --> 00:53:51,460
The 20 year old will be performing a forward three and a half somersaults in the pike position at three point.

738
00:53:51,539 --> 00:53:53,943
Oh, this is actually her highest degree of difficulty.

739
00:53:56,967 --> 00:53:58,670
It was a best dive in the prelims.

740
00:54:02,237 --> 00:54:07,364
Just waiting for that whistle confirmation that she's good to go and she's got it.

741
00:54:07,545 --> 00:54:08,606
So in her own time.

742
00:54:12,097 --> 00:54:13,998
No, and that's washed over again.

743
00:54:14,059 --> 00:54:21,347
So, well, the pressure coming to bear, that little bit of additional adrenaline, and it can make a huge difference to the dives.

744
00:54:21,367 --> 00:54:25,731
Sometimes when you tighten up in a competition, things just don't flow.

745
00:54:25,791 --> 00:54:37,585
She hit the end of the diving board, and she didn't throw in time, so the momentum of the jog down the pole has taken her out, and then she misses her spot.

746
00:54:37,605 --> 00:54:38,385
Pike is OK.

747
00:54:40,306 --> 00:54:41,748
It's been quite a few misses now.

748
00:54:42,909 --> 00:54:47,976
52.50 Not far off, but not quite there.

749
00:54:51,139 --> 00:54:54,182
Opportunities opening up, left, right and centre here.

750
00:54:54,262 --> 00:54:56,686
Can Georgia Ward take her chance?

751
00:54:57,005 --> 00:55:00,931
She's got the dive list, that high degree of difficulty to do it.

752
00:55:00,951 --> 00:55:06,657
Back three and a half somersaults in the tuck position at 3.3, the toughest dive in the competition.

753
00:55:14,094 --> 00:55:16,637
Oh, well done, Georgia.

754
00:55:16,657 --> 00:55:18,920
What a dive.

755
00:55:18,940 --> 00:55:19,960
I knew that was coming.

756
00:55:20,461 --> 00:55:23,664
The last two attempts, she has gone short.

757
00:55:23,684 --> 00:55:26,927
And I'm sure her coach has said, kick your feet up.

758
00:55:26,947 --> 00:55:28,610
Don't kick them back towards the ball.

759
00:55:28,630 --> 00:55:29,811
She did that.

760
00:55:29,831 --> 00:55:30,992
Gets the reach back.

761
00:55:32,054 --> 00:55:36,599
And with 3.3, this is going to be a phenomenal score.

762
00:55:36,619 --> 00:55:41,824
At the moment, the highest score has been 75 in the prelims.

763
00:55:42,630 --> 00:55:43,672
Can she go 80?

764
00:55:44,072 --> 00:55:47,255
That response from the crowd, massive, and she has done.

765
00:55:48,036 --> 00:55:52,219
80.85 puts Georgia Ward in the hunt for gold.

766
00:55:58,846 --> 00:56:01,547
Noemi Bakke for Italy.

767
00:56:02,670 --> 00:56:08,715
Three-time silver medalist in this event in 10-14, but she also won it back in 2011.

768
00:56:08,775 --> 00:56:11,878
So the platform has been kind.

769
00:56:12,617 --> 00:56:13,480
to the Italian.

770
00:56:14,280 --> 00:56:18,389
In with three and a half somersaults then round two to make up for that miss in round one.

771
00:56:23,320 --> 00:56:27,288
Oh, she really kicked hard for that and put everything into the entry.

772
00:56:27,568 --> 00:56:30,474
There was a booming sound as she goes through the water.

773
00:56:31,213 --> 00:56:33,498
And the tuck is really tight as well.

774
00:56:33,777 --> 00:56:42,652
Here, squeezing, chin very close to the knees, pops out of it, flat hand entry, and the boom goes around the whole of the poolside.

775
00:56:45,735 --> 00:56:47,699
Brilliant diving from Batki.

776
00:56:48,059 --> 00:56:49,481
Now we're cooking.

777
00:56:49,501 --> 00:56:50,364
Another 80.

778
00:56:51,264 --> 00:56:51,925
Look at that.

779
00:56:52,367 --> 00:56:56,512
And Batki goes to 125 for second place behind Georgia Ward.

780
00:56:57,539 --> 00:57:01,387
And that is the way to send the message out to the rest of this field.

781
00:57:02,789 --> 00:57:05,396
Katerina Petrikova then.

782
00:57:05,416 --> 00:57:06,498
Next for Russia.

783
00:57:07,179 --> 00:57:09,344
In with three and a half somersaults for her at 3.2.

784
00:57:09,945 --> 00:57:12,471
She has got a tough dive list as well.

785
00:57:13,172 --> 00:57:14,195
Everything in the threes.

786
00:57:15,318 --> 00:57:17,842
And she does the 3.3 in the next round.

787
00:57:22,108 --> 00:57:25,873
Oh, it's great diving, and this competition, Chris, has come alive.

788
00:57:26,775 --> 00:57:28,496
These are world-class dives.

789
00:57:30,219 --> 00:57:33,304
As we said in the earlier competitions, though, the standard is high.

790
00:57:33,324 --> 00:57:34,465
It's Olympic here.

791
00:57:34,565 --> 00:57:39,291
Everyone's been preparing very hard since last September, and you can see it.

792
00:57:41,554 --> 00:57:46,581
Gets the little roll on the entry, a bit of splash, but still a good dive.

793
00:57:49,530 --> 00:57:50,612
Brilliant.

794
00:57:50,632 --> 00:57:52,815
70.40 for Pechikova.

795
00:57:55,438 --> 00:58:00,184
And this one, this competition is warming up nicely.

796
00:58:01,164 --> 00:58:02,106
Maria Kojo then.

797
00:58:03,507 --> 00:58:09,335
Already has that gold medal with Maipan in the 10 meter synchro competition, but that was a little unexpected.

798
00:58:09,394 --> 00:58:16,163
And in the end, the medal came due to some misses by other teams, but she'll take it.

799
00:58:17,391 --> 00:58:22,418
Sports soldier by trade, but currently studying as a law and psychology student.

800
00:58:24,161 --> 00:58:28,927
And she's going to need all of that experience to put into this arm stand.

801
00:58:29,827 --> 00:58:32,992
Back twister.

802
00:58:33,012 --> 00:58:33,653
Well done.

803
00:58:33,833 --> 00:58:35,436
Well done.

804
00:58:35,456 --> 00:58:38,539
Another rip entry.

805
00:58:38,559 --> 00:58:42,445
3.2 degree of difficulty.

806
00:58:42,485 --> 00:58:46,150
She gets a push off her arms before going into the one and a half twist.

807
00:58:48,172 --> 00:58:49,074
That's good there.

808
00:58:49,293 --> 00:58:53,601
Now pulls forward, looks at the water, lines up just in time.

809
00:58:57,047 --> 00:58:58,570
What a dive.

810
00:58:58,590 --> 00:59:00,733
And that looked fabulous on that last slo-mo.

811
00:59:01,273 --> 00:59:02,597
And that's a fabulous score.

812
00:59:02,617 --> 00:59:05,260
76.80 takes it to 1.3980.

813
00:59:05,280 --> 00:59:12,693
5.05 off of the pace set at the moment by the Brit, Georgia Ward.

814
00:59:16,318 --> 00:59:19,121
Kristina Wasson will always follow Kojo in every round.

815
00:59:19,742 --> 00:59:21,505
Lovely start from the 17-year-old.

816
00:59:22,266 --> 00:59:24,068
Another 75 would do nicely.

817
00:59:26,431 --> 00:59:28,034
No, and it's not going to happen.

818
00:59:28,494 --> 00:59:30,476
There's the mistake from Wasson then.

819
00:59:30,496 --> 00:59:31,257
Washes it over.

820
00:59:31,297 --> 00:59:33,721
Exactly the same as the prelim.

821
00:59:33,760 --> 00:59:35,682
She hangs onto the pipe too long.

822
00:59:35,922 --> 00:59:39,728
The feet go up to the 10 meter and over onto her stomach.

823
00:59:40,112 --> 01:00:09,764
needs to be out now she's still in the pike and she finished something like five and a half meters there you can see the five meter board as she's coming out and just the feet have gone to the wrong place tough break for Wassen 30.45 dumps her down to ninth place with two still to come well Liliya Prokocuk in second position behind Wassen

824
01:00:10,014 --> 01:00:12,577
with her 70 pointer in the first round.

825
01:00:13,057 --> 01:00:14,898
Much better start than she made in the prelims.

826
01:00:15,239 --> 01:00:17,280
In with three and a half in the tuck position now.

827
01:00:17,320 --> 01:00:18,762
High degree of difficulty.

828
01:00:19,922 --> 01:00:21,003
Looking for the big score.

829
01:00:23,907 --> 01:00:26,309
And we get an enormous score.

830
01:00:26,329 --> 01:00:27,650
That's a fabulous dive.

831
01:00:27,949 --> 01:00:29,271
She finished so high on it.

832
01:00:29,291 --> 01:00:30,693
This is a hard dive.

833
01:00:31,213 --> 01:00:32,994
And she had so much time at the end.

834
01:00:33,655 --> 01:00:34,295
Double there.

835
01:00:35,416 --> 01:00:39,280
Now she finished above the five meter.

836
01:00:39,967 --> 01:00:41,731
We've already had 280 dives.

837
01:00:42,411 --> 01:00:44,855
This is on the same par as Georgia Ward.

838
01:00:48,661 --> 01:00:50,503
Astonishing stuff in round two.

839
01:00:50,684 --> 01:00:52,005
It's another 80.

840
01:00:52,025 --> 01:00:56,251
81-60 puts Prakopchuk in the lead.

841
01:00:56,271 --> 01:01:00,838
So she will move ahead of Georgia Ward by 8.75 points.

842
01:01:03,842 --> 01:01:06,347
Talk about pressure for Tonya Couch.

843
01:01:08,807 --> 01:01:11,612
blew everyone away for most of the prelim.

844
01:01:13,394 --> 01:01:23,268
Had an error at the end, which led a few athletes get closer to her, but came into this competition as the marginal favorite and has to produce some magic here.

845
01:01:24,251 --> 01:01:27,835
Arm stand back twister then.

846
01:01:27,856 --> 01:01:29,759
Antonio Couch is in business.

847
01:01:32,322 --> 01:01:37,971
Well, we've had some, this is one of the best rounds I've seen at Europeans for a long, long time.

848
01:01:40,532 --> 01:01:41,894
Nails it.

849
01:01:41,914 --> 01:01:47,023
So at the moment the highest score is 81.6.

850
01:01:47,043 --> 01:01:50,068
Well, her feet were better than the prelims, so this is going to be massive.

851
01:01:52,592 --> 01:01:55,557
Yeah, it's going to be 80.

852
01:01:56,539 --> 01:01:57,922
Oh, it's 86.4.

853
01:01:59,425 --> 01:02:05,594
Back into second position at 147.90 and just five points down on Lulia Prokopciuk.

854
01:02:05,675 --> 01:02:06,777
What a competition.

855
01:02:11,161 --> 01:02:13,885
A simple dive for Alea Kalanji.

856
01:02:13,925 --> 01:02:21,335
You'll see it on the replay, but unfortunately she has problems with the reverse dive family and has to stick to that.

857
01:02:21,594 --> 01:02:23,518
A very simple dive at 1.9.

858
01:02:23,617 --> 01:02:24,639
She's done it beautifully again.

859
01:02:25,760 --> 01:02:37,577
Yeah, she has, but because of that low degree of difficulty or come up as a very low score, somewhere around 40 points, she would have gone even higher with the score if she hadn't had that drift over at the end.

860
01:02:37,597 --> 01:02:40,340
39.90 for Kalanji.

861
01:02:41,130 --> 01:02:47,721
And that's the dive that is always going to cause us some problems until she builds some high degree of difficulty in.

862
01:02:48,963 --> 01:02:55,632
Well, Laura Moreno must be wondering what an earth is going on in this competition because it's all happening around her.

863
01:02:56,293 --> 01:02:58,436
Has not found a good divers yet.

864
01:02:59,458 --> 01:03:03,505
The French woman who finished in second place in 2015 in Rostock.

865
01:03:05,588 --> 01:03:09,753
She would dearly love to come to the party in round three with this back two and a half somersaults.

866
01:03:16,349 --> 01:03:17,570
Oh, why not?

867
01:03:17,590 --> 01:03:18,351
Why not?

868
01:03:18,371 --> 01:03:22,097
Another brilliant entry.

869
01:03:22,117 --> 01:03:24,862
Well, maybe this is going to be the round where she starts to pick up.

870
01:03:25,262 --> 01:03:25,784
Good jump.

871
01:03:26,244 --> 01:03:27,126
Looking with her head.

872
01:03:27,206 --> 01:03:28,869
You can see her head moving.

873
01:03:30,411 --> 01:03:38,965
Here, she looks at the end of the board, sees it, looks at the water, sees it, reaches back and sees it and disappears.

874
01:03:41,628 --> 01:03:45,693
Yes, what a lovely way of describing the process that the diver is going through, Chris.

875
01:03:45,773 --> 01:03:46,152
Brilliant.

876
01:03:46,474 --> 01:03:47,474
And that's a good score.

877
01:03:47,494 --> 01:03:49,777
73.95 for Laura Marino.

878
01:03:50,418 --> 01:03:54,443
A little collision with the camera operator, but she's happy.

879
01:03:54,882 --> 01:03:57,365
Wouldn't have been smiling if she'd got a 40, I can tell you.

880
01:03:58,487 --> 01:04:01,231
Now, Genevieve and Jeremy, keep your fingers crossed.

881
01:04:01,550 --> 01:04:06,657
Friday the 13th is a day that at the moment she would prefer to forget.

882
01:04:12,442 --> 01:04:17,528
No, it's still not happening, I'm afraid, for Genevieve.

883
01:04:17,548 --> 01:04:20,652
Well, for the first three quarters of the dive, it's fine.

884
01:04:21,054 --> 01:04:21,574
Good jump.

885
01:04:22,114 --> 01:04:25,920
Spot's well on the first somersault, but she doesn't pick up the second spot.

886
01:04:25,940 --> 01:04:26,661
Here it's good.

887
01:04:27,302 --> 01:04:30,085
But right here, she's looking in the wrong place.

888
01:04:30,126 --> 01:04:33,351
She should have seen the water and then pushed her feet out.

889
01:04:33,891 --> 01:04:34,873
She leaves it too late.

890
01:04:35,594 --> 01:04:36,215
It's gone over.

891
01:04:39,259 --> 01:04:40,760
Well, the smile once again.

892
01:04:41,838 --> 01:04:43,420
But it's looking a little tired now.

893
01:04:43,440 --> 01:04:49,108
33.35, still only managing to get to 62 marks after three rounds of diving.

894
01:04:50,971 --> 01:04:55,297
Celine Vando and then forward three and a half somersaults in the pike position at 3.0.

895
01:04:58,280 --> 01:05:07,474
Diving well, but the class around here from some of the big names at the moment eclipsing anything that she's managed to do.

896
01:05:09,496 --> 01:05:12,400
So round three needs to be big for the Dutch woman.

897
01:05:15,344 --> 01:05:16,184
It's a good dive.

898
01:05:16,525 --> 01:05:20,530
A little bit of a depth charge going up after the entry, but she'll take that.

899
01:05:21,811 --> 01:05:23,454
Yeah, this is correct.

900
01:05:23,474 --> 01:05:24,135
She jumps up.

901
01:05:24,615 --> 01:05:26,177
The one in prelim jumped forward.

902
01:05:26,798 --> 01:05:30,483
But as she's coming out, the whole of the middle of her body is loose.

903
01:05:30,503 --> 01:05:31,925
She's not holding the stomach tight.

904
01:05:31,965 --> 01:05:33,186
The back goes loose.

905
01:05:34,208 --> 01:05:39,114
And the water then hits you, and your body concertinas.

906
01:05:39,668 --> 01:05:41,349
And that's why this flash has come up.

907
01:05:47,297 --> 01:05:50,121
I'm still waiting for that mark.

908
01:05:50,282 --> 01:05:51,083
And 58.50.

909
01:05:51,143 --> 01:05:58,193
If that's as bad as it gets, then it's not going to be too bad for Celine Van doing.

910
01:05:58,893 --> 01:06:01,777
But in this kind of company at the moment, it isn't good enough.

911
01:06:03,125 --> 01:06:04,786
That's Nuzlic then next.

912
01:06:04,806 --> 01:06:08,132
9th position after two rounds.

913
01:06:09,072 --> 01:06:12,257
Forward twister, so two and a half somersaults then with a single twist.

914
01:06:12,297 --> 01:06:16,342
Let's see where she puts the twist in to this particular dive.

915
01:06:23,050 --> 01:06:26,735
So the twist straight away then pulls into the somersaults and a nice entry.

916
01:06:29,280 --> 01:06:31,244
Yeah, just a small jump forward.

917
01:06:31,965 --> 01:06:39,375
Yeah, as she landed on the board, her body bent forward there and as she's throwing down rather than forwards.

918
01:06:40,556 --> 01:06:41,577
Gets a good entry though.

919
01:06:42,318 --> 01:06:45,784
Just a little bit sloppy on the start and just going into the pike.

