01:06:46,284 --> 01:06:47,525
Could have a little deeper pike.

921
01:06:50,369 --> 01:06:53,735
Once again, coach Ivanenko comes across for a chap.

922
01:06:53,755 --> 01:06:57,599
60.90.

923
01:06:58,086 --> 01:07:01,871
That's Narslik giving a good account of herself.

924
01:07:01,891 --> 01:07:08,958
Now Georgia Ward, you get the feeling actually that it was Georgia that really kicked this competition into life in round two.

925
01:07:10,260 --> 01:07:12,302
Absolutely nailed her back three and a half.

926
01:07:13,262 --> 01:07:16,726
Went into the lead and everybody found it difficult to live with her from there.

927
01:07:18,088 --> 01:07:25,597
So arm stand back to somersaults with one and a half twists for Georgia Ward in a home pull.

928
01:07:26,597 --> 01:07:27,739
Another good dive here.

929
01:07:28,005 --> 01:07:29,849
And she is definitely in business.

930
01:07:36,222 --> 01:07:37,043
Oh, superb.

931
01:07:37,384 --> 01:07:41,911
That little separation of the legs as she came away from the platform, but got it all back together.

932
01:07:42,132 --> 01:07:44,918
Yeah, it's so minor that it's not going to affect.

933
01:07:46,112 --> 01:07:47,034
the judge's score.

934
01:07:47,335 --> 01:07:50,579
The loose body going through the water will drop her down a little bit.

935
01:07:51,039 --> 01:07:53,623
She went 67 points in the prelim.

936
01:07:53,643 --> 01:07:55,364
This is just about the same dive.

937
01:07:55,846 --> 01:07:56,827
Very good in the air.

938
01:07:57,148 --> 01:07:59,831
Bit splashy going through the water, so it'll be a similar score.

939
01:08:01,092 --> 01:08:03,996
67 points will keep her on track, and that's where she is.

940
01:08:04,016 --> 01:08:06,599
67-2-0 for 212.05.

941
01:08:06,800 --> 01:08:09,344
Ward moves back into the lead.

942
01:08:09,384 --> 01:08:15,731
Noemi Bakke, then.

943
01:08:16,672 --> 01:08:28,353
from a Hungarian diver that moved to Italy back in 2005, coached by Mami Bolyanaj, the 1992 Olympian from Barcelona.

944
01:08:30,155 --> 01:08:34,863
Has been superb in this competition in previous years, but isn't happening for her at the moment.

945
01:08:36,407 --> 01:08:38,310
Reverse two and a half then for Noemi.

946
01:08:40,653 --> 01:08:41,954
Well, wonderful.

947
01:08:42,015 --> 01:08:43,877
How high did she go off the platform there?

948
01:08:44,537 --> 01:08:46,000
And always in control.

949
01:08:46,020 --> 01:08:46,860
She didn't hold back.

950
01:08:46,921 --> 01:08:47,721
She's standing there.

951
01:08:47,762 --> 01:08:48,684
She thought about it.

952
01:08:48,764 --> 01:08:49,585
She visualized it.

953
01:08:49,805 --> 01:08:52,889
And then she jumped.

954
01:08:52,908 --> 01:08:56,274
She was kicking out at seven and a half meters.

955
01:08:56,293 --> 01:08:58,596
The double here, seven and a half meters kick.

956
01:08:59,037 --> 01:09:02,061
She floats around for six meters.

957
01:09:02,362 --> 01:09:04,484
There's the seven meter right next to her.

958
01:09:05,286 --> 01:09:06,728
And then she reaches back.

959
01:09:07,822 --> 01:09:08,443
What a dive.

960
01:09:08,622 --> 01:09:09,363
Into the 70s.

961
01:09:10,064 --> 01:09:13,029
And remember, that's a lower degree of difficulty at 2.8.

962
01:09:14,631 --> 01:09:16,255
So that score is fabulous.

963
01:09:16,335 --> 01:09:17,716
And Mum is happy.

964
01:09:20,862 --> 01:09:24,166
Katerina Petrikova then in fifth position at the moment.

965
01:09:26,310 --> 01:09:31,197
Sometimes in the shadow of her synchro partner, Timoshenina.

966
01:09:32,998 --> 01:10:01,841
has a chance to shine here because Timoshenina failed to get through the prelims so back three and a half this is her toughest dive equal toughest dive in the competition oh and it's a nasty one so again another big miss and this time it's from the russian missed it in the previous only scored 40 something points on it the jump is good but it's spinning too slow she hangs on as long as possible and then goes over

967
01:10:02,868 --> 01:10:07,472
It's not accelerating, it's just dropping like a stone, and barely time to come out.

968
01:10:08,854 --> 01:10:10,735
She'll be lucky to get 40 on this one.

969
01:10:12,537 --> 01:10:13,800
That was even worse than the prelim.

970
01:10:14,460 --> 01:10:17,863
Yeah, it's just 37.95 then for Petrkova.

971
01:10:19,826 --> 01:10:24,610
A real shame for her, and that's probably the medal challenge done for the Russian.

972
01:10:24,690 --> 01:10:28,414
But never say never, anything can happen where platform diving is concerned.

973
01:10:28,435 --> 01:10:31,018
And it did in the prelims.

974
01:10:32,264 --> 01:10:35,168
A few big names missing out, a few big names nearly missing out.

975
01:10:36,652 --> 01:10:39,176
Marie Courget then, the 27-year-old German.

976
01:10:40,998 --> 01:10:43,423
Trains in Berlin coached by Jan Kretschmar.

977
01:10:45,728 --> 01:10:46,708
And that's really nice.

978
01:10:47,310 --> 01:10:52,720
But on a day she's a very tidy, very efficient diver and that's what she's bringing to this final.

979
01:10:53,627 --> 01:11:01,697
She finished in 12th place last year, but she's got three bronze medals in this event from 11, 12 and 2013.

980
01:11:02,018 --> 01:11:04,039
It was a good dive.

981
01:11:05,202 --> 01:11:06,762
It's a lower degree of difficulty.

982
01:11:07,264 --> 01:11:13,530
I was watching her toes as she passed the board and it was just about safe enough, any closer than she would have touched.

983
01:11:14,672 --> 01:11:18,436
Solid score, 60.20 to reach the 200 mark.

984
01:11:19,261 --> 01:11:21,344
after three rounds of five.

985
01:11:23,065 --> 01:11:26,690
Slightly disconsolate look from Christina Arsene.

986
01:11:29,073 --> 01:11:31,117
There she went from first to 11th.

987
01:11:32,137 --> 01:11:33,720
And that's not going to keep anyone happy.

988
01:11:34,381 --> 01:11:36,463
So Arsene armstand dive for her.

989
01:11:36,623 --> 01:11:39,448
Armstand back to somersaults, one and a half twists.

990
01:11:40,208 --> 01:11:42,551
And that gives her a degree of difficulty of 3.2.

991
01:11:44,253 --> 01:11:45,876
So this is the kind of dive

992
01:11:46,479 --> 01:11:56,496
if she gets the entry that she was getting in the prelims that could put her back in contention.

993
01:11:56,536 --> 01:12:01,403
It's good, it's good, but it's not going to push her up too far on the leaderboard.

994
01:12:01,944 --> 01:12:04,108
There's a better handstand this time in the prelim.

995
01:12:04,148 --> 01:12:07,472
She didn't get to that completely straight position.

996
01:12:09,015 --> 01:12:12,740
Now she is just twisting all the way down to the pole.

997
01:12:13,430 --> 01:12:16,554
But it's an entry, it's going to score really well.

998
01:12:18,015 --> 01:12:24,744
Technique isn't that brilliant off the platform, not enough jump and the twist took so long to get into.

999
01:12:24,765 --> 01:12:34,938
70.40 then, takes her to 176.05, so she will improve her position from 11th to round about 9th.

1000
01:12:36,340 --> 01:12:42,188
Just a reminder, Georgia Ward leads for Great Britain on 212.05.

1001
01:12:43,162 --> 01:12:48,208
Prokopchuk and her compatriot Tonya Couch can get past her.

1002
01:12:53,114 --> 01:12:58,421
And with diving like this, the defence of her title is starting to look very, very good indeed.

1003
01:12:58,560 --> 01:13:02,265
That's a great dive on that back two and a half.

1004
01:13:02,286 --> 01:13:03,346
What a jump.

1005
01:13:03,367 --> 01:13:03,868
Spots.

1006
01:13:05,649 --> 01:13:09,154
Just collapses a little bit going through the water.

1007
01:13:09,505 --> 01:13:10,445
Here it's good.

1008
01:13:12,149 --> 01:13:12,869
Reaches back.

1009
01:13:13,109 --> 01:13:17,015
She needs only 58 points to go into the lead.

1010
01:13:19,600 --> 01:13:23,364
I guess she'll get that.

1011
01:13:23,386 --> 01:13:28,894
And the four-time European 10-meter champion moves back into top spot.

1012
01:13:28,953 --> 01:13:29,954
2.2175.

1013
01:13:30,095 --> 01:13:35,243
So that's a 9.7 advantage.

1014
01:13:35,627 --> 01:13:41,520
over Georgia Ward in second, 21.7 advantage over Maria Kujo in third.

1015
01:13:42,501 --> 01:13:46,789
And Tonya Kouch has got this tough position, the pressure keeps passing down.

1016
01:13:46,989 --> 01:13:49,173
Inward three and a half then for Tonya at 3.2.

1017
01:13:49,375 --> 01:13:57,130
And she will keep pace with that dive.

1018
01:13:57,886 --> 01:14:00,189
She needs 73 points to go and lead.

1019
01:14:00,210 --> 01:14:01,192
I'm not quite sure.

1020
01:14:01,212 --> 01:14:03,896
With that entry, she pulls her chin down on the end.

1021
01:14:05,739 --> 01:14:06,761
But that start is good.

1022
01:14:07,061 --> 01:14:10,287
Finishes high, but just lost it on the entry.

1023
01:14:10,328 --> 01:14:12,631
Need to have the confidence to keep stretching.

1024
01:14:13,314 --> 01:14:16,800
She pushes here, and you see the arms are out of line.

1025
01:14:17,902 --> 01:14:19,725
So the judges will mark her down for that.

1026
01:14:20,920 --> 01:14:23,743
So probably sub-70, but by how much?

1027
01:14:23,923 --> 01:14:25,966
Well, just under five points.

1028
01:14:26,065 --> 01:14:33,876
So Tonya Couch does move into second at 2.1350, just ahead of Georgia Ward, but it's the defending champion Prokopchuk that leads.

1029
01:14:36,279 --> 01:14:46,371
Back just in time for another rip entry, this time from Laura Mourinho, the French number one, after that arm stand, back two somersaults and one and a half twists.

1030
01:14:46,890 --> 01:14:51,158
Another lovely entry, using the bend knee to flick off.

1031
01:14:51,779 --> 01:14:54,143
A lot of the ladies are just leaning off.

1032
01:14:54,563 --> 01:14:56,827
That's why I like that technique.

1033
01:14:56,846 --> 01:15:00,051
Gets a little bit of extra rotation and a fast twist.

1034
01:15:00,552 --> 01:15:04,338
But it's the entry, little splash, that's given her the 73 points.

1035
01:15:04,720 --> 01:15:08,145
OK, moves to 260.15 after that 73.60.

1036
01:15:08,506 --> 01:15:14,215
So a couple of good rounds there from Laura Marino, and she's kind of back in business.

1037
01:15:15,307 --> 01:15:20,655
but needs to keep it at the highest possible level if she's going to be in with a shout of a place on the podium.

1038
01:15:20,676 --> 01:15:22,680
Now, come on, Genevieve.

1039
01:15:22,699 --> 01:15:24,242
17-year-old from Lithuania.

1040
01:15:24,823 --> 01:15:26,385
Reverse two-and-a-half somersaults.

1041
01:15:26,605 --> 01:15:27,506
Needs an entry.

1042
01:15:29,689 --> 01:15:31,172
Needs to get some confidence back.

1043
01:15:33,395 --> 01:15:36,360
And it's just not going to happen for her this evening.

1044
01:15:36,381 --> 01:15:38,944
And you sometimes get competitions like this, Chris.

1045
01:15:39,005 --> 01:15:40,927
It doesn't matter what you do, it doesn't work.

1046
01:15:41,296 --> 01:15:49,188
Sometimes when you've got experience, if you're spinning at a different rate in the competition, you know to make adjustments and that's what's happened here.

1047
01:15:49,708 --> 01:15:57,761
She's jumped a little higher than normal, she's spinning faster than normal, but she's done the same kick out that she would do in practice and that is why she's gone over.

1048
01:15:58,002 --> 01:16:01,707
The extra adrenaline she hasn't taken into account.

1049
01:16:01,728 --> 01:16:07,235
Still a high school student back in the USA but retained her Lithuanian passport when she moved there.

1050
01:16:07,738 --> 01:16:14,010
at two years of age and has to put this one down to experience, I'm afraid, this evening.

1051
01:16:15,532 --> 01:16:21,662
Celine Van Leeuwen has dived very well and seventh the best that she can manage at the moment.

1052
01:16:24,127 --> 01:16:28,914
This then her joint toughest dive, arm stand back to somersaults with one and a half twists.

1053
01:16:29,896 --> 01:16:33,443
So like her back twister in the first round, it's worth 3.2.

1054
01:16:34,452 --> 01:16:36,034
in terms of degree of difficulty.

1055
01:16:36,234 --> 01:16:38,177
Is this the dive that puts her back in business?

1056
01:16:43,967 --> 01:16:45,149
Not quite, I'm afraid.

1057
01:16:45,250 --> 01:16:51,600
Again, just going over on the end and judges will certainly deduct for that.

1058
01:16:51,867 --> 01:16:58,438
Not only did she lean, but she had the bent knee flick, which just gave her a little too much rotation.

1059
01:16:58,938 --> 01:17:03,104
When she pikes down, she couldn't stop it, digs the head in as well.

1060
01:17:03,365 --> 01:17:06,090
That actually accelerated those legs going over.

1061
01:17:07,372 --> 01:17:08,354
That would be a miss for her.

1062
01:17:10,136 --> 01:17:10,837
52.80.

1063
01:17:11,859 --> 01:17:14,222
It is a miss.

1064
01:17:14,262 --> 01:17:17,488
Van Doorn will not be able to recover from that.

1065
01:17:17,547 --> 01:17:19,190
So that's her medal challenge done.

1066
01:17:20,774 --> 01:17:24,280
Hannah Krasnowska then for Ukraine.

1067
01:17:26,323 --> 01:17:32,416
Again, dive very solidly, but in this kind of company, eighth position, the best that she can manage at the moment.

1068
01:17:35,542 --> 01:17:41,112
Unlikely to match her fifth place from 2015, which was a brilliant performance.

1069
01:17:50,457 --> 01:17:53,220
No it's very strange start to that back two and a half.

1070
01:17:53,520 --> 01:18:04,717
Yeah she keeps her knees bent so right here her legs are bent and then she finally straightens up those legs for the second part of the dive but that's an untidy pipe there.

1071
01:18:05,418 --> 01:18:15,434
Here doesn't spot the water that looks to me more like a guess rather than using your eyes to see where to come around where to come out and she's gone right over.

1072
01:18:15,453 --> 01:18:19,840
2.19.90 that

1073
01:18:20,630 --> 01:18:23,153
rolling score and that's a miss at 43.50.

1074
01:18:24,215 --> 01:18:28,039
Lauren Marino leads for France then on 2.61.5.

1075
01:18:29,221 --> 01:18:37,752
Georgia Ward will be looking to go past her and by some distance with this fourth round dive.

1076
01:18:37,893 --> 01:18:41,859
Forward three and a half somersaults in the pike position then her lowest degree of difficulty.

1077
01:18:41,899 --> 01:18:43,100
This needs to be perfect.

1078
01:18:46,185 --> 01:18:48,448
Oh and again just washes over at the end.

1079
01:18:48,547 --> 01:18:50,130
Oh she'll be frustrated with that

1080
01:18:50,819 --> 01:18:52,661
Oh, that's a real shame.

1081
01:18:52,680 --> 01:18:55,664
She only needed 48 points to go in the lead.

1082
01:18:58,649 --> 01:19:00,511
Well, she's got such a good take-off here.

1083
01:19:01,091 --> 01:19:02,033
Pulls him well there.

1084
01:19:02,073 --> 01:19:04,176
Needed to be out already.

1085
01:19:08,202 --> 01:19:10,024
Yeah.

1086
01:19:10,043 --> 01:19:11,947
Now, she's nailed that entry.

1087
01:19:11,966 --> 01:19:13,788
She'll get an extra 15 points.

1088
01:19:14,545 --> 01:19:15,145
Oh, she had.

1089
01:19:15,386 --> 01:19:23,555
Yeah, coach Figueredo watching on, and 57 gives her the lead at 269.05, but it's not the kind of advancement that she was looking for.

1090
01:19:23,576 --> 01:19:28,680
If that is Georgia Ward's miss, then OK, she'll probably take that one.

1091
01:19:30,503 --> 01:19:32,365
Big dive to come in the final round for her.

1092
01:19:36,970 --> 01:19:43,759
For Noemi Bakke, so far, this has not been her European championships.

1093
01:19:45,172 --> 01:19:52,595
Fifth position at the moment, so outside the medals, but still has the degree of difficulty to force a way onto the podium.

1094
01:19:55,364 --> 01:19:57,731
She needs 70 points to catch Georgia Ward.

1095
01:20:04,934 --> 01:20:11,703
No and that just was one of those classic arm stand dives where the diver just falls straight off the platform and into the water.

1096
01:20:12,063 --> 01:20:16,630
Yeah she needs to go back in the gym to work on this to get the timing.

1097
01:20:16,670 --> 01:20:25,220
She just hasn't got the timing and that's why it looks so awkward.

1098
01:20:25,240 --> 01:20:26,021
That's a miss for her.

1099
01:20:27,404 --> 01:20:29,726
You can see how low she finishes to the water.

1100
01:20:31,411 --> 01:20:33,873
Not a great dive to watch, not a great score to get.

1101
01:20:33,894 --> 01:20:37,378
54-4-0, back is challenged, falters again.

1102
01:20:44,408 --> 01:20:47,592
Ekaterina Petrikova, one miss, too many.

1103
01:20:48,835 --> 01:20:56,085
And she's down in 10th position, but in this kind of competition and in this kind of company, one miss is too many.

1104
01:20:59,170 --> 01:21:02,132
Slightly different arm stand position here.

1105
01:21:02,594 --> 01:21:07,520
Facing the pull with her back for this two somersaults single twist at 3.1.

1106
01:21:08,400 --> 01:21:09,322
Unusual dive this.

1107
01:21:15,649 --> 01:21:20,034
Both she and Timoshenina have the same technique for the push-off and it's really effective.

1108
01:21:20,055 --> 01:21:23,018
Yeah, the hips go first and then the feet flick.

1109
01:21:23,943 --> 01:21:28,448
So there's the hips and then the flick, then the single twist and look at the water.

1110
01:21:30,029 --> 01:21:31,051
Yeah, it's a good technique.

1111
01:21:32,351 --> 01:21:34,734
Maybe just bending the arms a little too much.

1112
01:21:35,355 --> 01:21:38,519
You only have to relax your arms rather than bend them right down.

1113
01:21:40,581 --> 01:21:42,182
It's actually quite a complicated dive.

1114
01:21:44,104 --> 01:21:45,086
And that's a good score.

1115
01:21:45,106 --> 01:21:51,873
68-20 takes it to 2.4405, so partial recovery once again from Petrkova.

1116
01:21:53,422 --> 01:21:57,349
Now, Chris, you think that Maria Cujo could be the danger.

1117
01:21:57,448 --> 01:21:59,993
Back two and a half somersaults from her in the pike position.

1118
01:22:01,113 --> 01:22:04,319
Yeah, she only needs 69 points to take the lead.

1119
01:22:05,921 --> 01:22:08,585
And she went, she actually missed this dive in the prelims.

1120
01:22:08,664 --> 01:22:09,326
Only got 56.

1121
01:22:09,365 --> 01:22:15,154
She's got to remember to come out in time, not let the dive go over.

1122
01:22:18,259 --> 01:22:19,621
Oh, it's gone over again.

1123
01:22:19,661 --> 01:22:22,484
Almost carbon copy of the prelims.

1124
01:22:23,444 --> 01:22:26,047
Yeah, you should be able to make an adjustment in the prelims.

1125
01:22:26,109 --> 01:22:30,416
If you're going to go short, you have the same sort of pressure because you're wanting to make the top 12.

1126
01:22:31,837 --> 01:22:33,801
You need to remember to come out early.

1127
01:22:34,523 --> 01:22:35,845
Looks at the water too late.

1128
01:22:36,565 --> 01:22:38,970
It's bypassed her and out too late.

1129
01:22:38,989 --> 01:22:39,851
So right over.

1130
01:22:44,680 --> 01:22:48,185
42.05 and that miss, I'm afraid.

1131
01:22:49,027 --> 01:22:53,393
is going to put the lid on Kujo's challenge and less others miss around her.

1132
01:22:55,595 --> 01:23:02,685
For Vasan, same situation as Kujo except her miss occurred on the last dive.

1133
01:23:03,606 --> 01:23:09,293
So Vasan trying to repair the damage with this forward three and a half somersaults in the pike position.

1134
01:23:13,300 --> 01:23:16,384
Oh, that's more like the entries we saw from her in the prelims.

1135
01:23:17,578 --> 01:23:21,923
It's amazing that she could get down with no splash, even with the dive going over.

1136
01:23:22,185 --> 01:23:23,206
So it's going to score well.

1137
01:23:23,845 --> 01:23:27,610
Yeah, she attacks the end of the diving board.

1138
01:23:27,631 --> 01:23:28,731
Pulling in well here.

1139
01:23:29,613 --> 01:23:34,899
Again, the technique of holding down on the lower part of the legs rather than around the back of the knees.

1140
01:23:36,601 --> 01:23:38,283
It doesn't matter if you get an entry like that.

1141
01:23:39,484 --> 01:23:41,847
Good awareness, good scoop under the water.

1142
01:23:42,283 --> 01:23:44,927
to save that dive and that's a good score.

1143
01:23:45,007 --> 01:23:52,538
67.50 puts Varsan temporarily up to fifth position with two divers still to come in this round.

1144
01:23:55,122 --> 01:24:03,074
Arm stand back, three somersaults in the tuck position for Lulia Prokopchuk for the joint highest degree of difficulty in the competition at 3.3.

1145
01:24:03,336 --> 01:24:06,720
This is the big dive for her, Chris.

1146
01:24:06,761 --> 01:24:09,625
If she gets this right, gold and defensive title is on.

1147
01:24:10,177 --> 01:24:12,782
It's only a 75.9 in the prelim.

1148
01:24:12,822 --> 01:24:15,386
She only needs 48 points to go ahead of Georgia.

1149
01:24:21,835 --> 01:24:23,717
Oh, it's beautiful from Prokopchuk.

1150
01:24:23,738 --> 01:24:26,542
She has not missed a beat this evening.

1151
01:24:26,563 --> 01:24:30,547
Well, if she gets eight, which it's worth, it's going to be 75 again.

1152
01:24:31,569 --> 01:24:32,912
Strong kick out.

1153
01:24:34,478 --> 01:24:36,644
Oh, this is even better than the prelims.

1154
01:24:36,703 --> 01:24:43,963
Look, sharp kick, reaches back, tightens her body, quick save under the water, stops the feet kicking over.

1155
01:24:44,284 --> 01:24:45,408
That's the way to go through.

1156
01:24:45,448 --> 01:24:47,252
She's always known what she's doing.

1157
01:24:47,273 --> 01:24:50,360
She saw that triple somersault from about four meters up.

1158
01:24:50,762 --> 01:24:54,627
Chris Snowd loved it, but more importantly, the judges loved it.

1159
01:24:54,648 --> 01:24:56,730
84.15 takes her over 300.

1160
01:24:56,751 --> 01:24:59,493
305.90 leads.

1161
01:24:59,573 --> 01:25:05,922
She's just put 36 points between her and George Ward in second place, and she's done it again.

1162
01:25:06,243 --> 01:25:11,990
She's passed all the pressure down the line to the 26-year-old Brit, Tonya Couch.

1163
01:25:13,431 --> 01:25:17,698
Back, twister then for Tonya at 3.2, just to stay in touch.

1164
01:25:21,037 --> 01:25:23,421
Oh, what a response from Tonya Couch.

1165
01:25:24,442 --> 01:25:26,345
Yeah, the pressure hasn't affected her at all.

1166
01:25:26,364 --> 01:25:27,927
They're still making her sharp.

1167
01:25:29,810 --> 01:25:36,622
She won't be able to catch Lida 92 points ahead, but that's going to still give her a chance.

1168
01:25:38,505 --> 01:25:44,793
If she misses, Tonya and even Georgia will have a chance on that final round.

1169
01:25:46,117 --> 01:25:47,078
Great fourth dive.

1170
01:25:47,546 --> 01:25:50,189
Couch looking to stay within touching distance, and she does.

1171
01:25:50,210 --> 01:25:52,872
72 marks takes her to 285.50.

1172
01:25:53,153 --> 01:26:00,961
That means she's just over 20 points behind Lulia Prokopciuk with one round of diving in this 10-meter final to go.

1173
01:26:01,020 --> 01:26:09,729
So Prokopciuk, the defending champion, leads, and she's got a handy cushion ahead of Couch and Ward, the two Brits in second and third.

1174
01:26:10,551 --> 01:26:12,592
One round then, left to come.

1175
01:26:12,573 --> 01:26:17,898
And one round of real drama, I'm sure, in store for us here in London.

1176
01:26:25,423 --> 01:26:30,948
Well, we teed this competition up at the start of the evening as potential drama, and it's exactly what we've got.

1177
01:26:33,390 --> 01:26:38,935
Last round of dives, then, in the women's 10-meter final at this 2016 European Championships.

1178
01:26:38,996 --> 01:26:41,618
Eli Kalonji, 18-year-old from

1179
01:26:42,273 --> 01:26:44,886
Paris has given a really good account of herself.

1180
01:26:44,926 --> 01:26:49,009
This to sign off their no medal tonight for a light, but it's a really good performance.

1181
01:26:51,114 --> 01:26:52,997
And she's been solid tonight.

1182
01:26:53,016 --> 01:26:53,637
She really has.

1183
01:26:53,898 --> 01:26:56,942
She has a unique sound to her entries.

1184
01:26:57,382 --> 01:26:59,744
It's not even quite a tearing sound.

1185
01:27:00,206 --> 01:27:03,310
It's just strange noise.

1186
01:27:03,329 --> 01:27:05,252
It's more of a thud, isn't it?

1187
01:27:05,271 --> 01:27:06,873
Yeah, but it's mesmerizing.

1188
01:27:07,253 --> 01:27:14,863
So clearly she's not as experienced as the other divers, but she looks quite poetic with her dives anyway.

1189
01:27:15,264 --> 01:27:20,109
And then you get this really strange, solid sound on the entry.

1190
01:27:20,409 --> 01:27:22,592
I do like that.

1191
01:27:22,613 --> 01:27:27,140
Moves to 2, 7, 9, 3, 0 for Kalonji.

1192
01:27:29,123 --> 01:27:31,287
And that's really good work from the 18-year-old.

1193
01:27:31,346 --> 01:27:32,309
Great experience.

1194
01:27:37,436 --> 01:27:43,667
Compatriot Laura Marino has already experienced a silver medal at these championships back in 2015.

1195
01:27:45,487 --> 01:27:48,390
But for her today, it just hasn't quite happened.

1196
01:27:48,650 --> 01:27:57,262
So back and forth at the moment, meaning this back two and a half somersaults with one and a half twists has to be the best that she can make it.

1197
01:27:58,463 --> 01:28:05,173
If she can get up into the high 70s, 80s, maybe there's a chance.

1198
01:28:05,194 --> 01:28:07,355
Oh no, just very short.

1199
01:28:08,398 --> 01:28:11,721
Yeah, when she was on the platform, the arms didn't swing up over her head.

1200
01:28:12,002 --> 01:28:13,704
She looked very rigid here.

1201
01:28:14,782 --> 01:28:36,097
then going forward into the plaque after the twist it's just too low to the water yeah very slow on the somersault she tried to stay into the plaque as long as she could but couldn't get around to the vertical position she was nine points behind georgia who was in third place at the end of round four and after her full

1202
01:28:36,448 --> 01:28:37,711
Five rounds of diving.

1203
01:28:37,751 --> 01:28:42,056
She's only eight points ahead of Prakopchuk, who's had four rounds.

1204
01:28:42,077 --> 01:28:43,538
So that puts it into context.

1205
01:28:43,759 --> 01:28:48,546
It's unlikely to be a medal for Marino this evening.

1206
01:28:48,565 --> 01:28:53,813
Genevieve Green-Anjirame, then, of Lithuania, the 17-year-old, still smiling.

1207
01:28:54,234 --> 01:28:55,916
The crowd have responded really well to her.

1208
01:28:55,956 --> 01:28:57,979
She's had a torrid time tonight.

1209
01:28:58,219 --> 01:28:59,942
Started off in the first round poorly.

1210
01:28:59,962 --> 01:29:03,806
That's knocked her confidence and just wants an entry in this final dive.

1211
01:29:05,947 --> 01:29:07,588
And she's got it at last.

1212
01:29:07,609 --> 01:29:09,770
Well done to Genevieve Anjarami.

1213
01:29:10,171 --> 01:29:12,953
Yeah, the highest score she's had at this point was 43.

1214
01:29:13,014 --> 01:29:15,095
She's got a 33, a 19, and an 8.

1215
01:29:17,018 --> 01:29:21,301
But finally, this is a dive that is worthy of the European Championship.

1216
01:29:21,582 --> 01:29:23,465
Good jump, lovely pike there.

1217
01:29:24,125 --> 01:29:24,746
Locks out.

1218
01:29:26,386 --> 01:29:31,011
It's a shame it's a low degree of difficulty, but they'll go more than 43 points.

1219
01:29:31,032 --> 01:29:35,936
What they can't take away from her is the fact that she's finished 12th in a European Championship.

1220
01:29:36,743 --> 01:29:39,046
And that's something certainly to brag about.

1221
01:29:41,029 --> 01:29:43,893
So Anjarami signs off with a good one.

1222
01:29:45,715 --> 01:29:48,599
Celine Van Doorn will want to be doing the same.

1223
01:29:50,502 --> 01:29:56,329
Best finish that she's had in this competition was last year and that was a ninth place.

1224
01:29:56,789 --> 01:30:00,055
So a good dive here and she could improve on that.

1225
01:30:02,818 --> 01:30:04,000
Qualified in ninth.

1226
01:30:05,194 --> 01:30:09,862
She came ninth last year and she's in ninth at the moment.

1227
01:30:09,881 --> 01:30:17,213
Back two and a half then for Celine.

1228
01:30:17,234 --> 01:30:22,882
Oh, it's a nice finish but she keeps throwing up that plume of splash when she goes through the water.

1229
01:30:23,047 --> 01:30:25,011
Yeah, that's not because of the takeoff.

1230
01:30:25,032 --> 01:30:25,573
This is good.

1231
01:30:26,033 --> 01:30:26,755
The pike is good.

1232
01:30:27,315 --> 01:30:30,020
But she just doesn't reach back enough with her hands.

1233
01:30:30,702 --> 01:30:34,649
It's almost like her shoulders are too tight and it's an effort to get the arms back there.

1234
01:30:35,369 --> 01:30:36,813
Needs to be reaching back there.

1235
01:30:36,872 --> 01:30:37,554
Doesn't do that.

1236
01:30:37,594 --> 01:30:42,643
The arms are in front of the ears and the body just collapses a little bit.

1237
01:30:44,902 --> 01:30:47,626
56.55 then for Van Doorn.

1238
01:30:47,645 --> 01:30:54,113
That little clunk you heard on the microphone then, that is my co-commentator Chris Snow basically demonstrating everything he talks about.

1239
01:30:54,215 --> 01:30:56,438
It's an animated commentary box, I can tell you.

1240
01:30:56,898 --> 01:30:57,779
I'm like the Italians.

1241
01:31:00,042 --> 01:31:07,292
Oh, they've had a good week, the Italians, and it might still get better as well with Delape and Cagnotto to go in the three-meter synchro later this week.

1242
01:31:08,092 --> 01:31:09,454
Now back to this competition.

1243
01:31:09,916 --> 01:31:12,538
Krasnozlic to sign off for Ukraine.

1244
01:31:12,939 --> 01:31:14,402
She's had a solid night this evening.

1245
01:31:25,942 --> 01:31:27,182
No, bad take-off.

1246
01:31:27,884 --> 01:31:29,865
How did she find that entry?

1247
01:31:29,886 --> 01:31:31,947
Where did that come from?

1248
01:31:31,966 --> 01:31:35,310
Feels like there's oil on the end of the diving board and she just slipped off.

1249
01:31:35,331 --> 01:31:37,533
She didn't get any jump, just slides there.

1250
01:31:38,193 --> 01:31:39,033
Kicks good though.

1251
01:31:39,875 --> 01:31:41,195
And the entry's fine as well.

1252
01:31:44,158 --> 01:31:49,182
Well, if she can get that start better, the judges won't be marking her down.

1253
01:31:49,523 --> 01:31:50,944
That'll be a 70-pointer.

1254
01:31:51,685 --> 01:31:54,547
The entry, though, will get still some good scores.

1255
01:31:55,387 --> 01:32:07,359
64-4-0 for Hanna Krasnozlic to finish off and acknowledges the applause from the crowd although some of that applause very definitely directed towards this young woman.

1256
01:32:07,378 --> 01:32:10,521
Georgia Ward then another big moment for her.

1257
01:32:10,542 --> 01:32:18,770
Already had one big moment in the team competition diving for that bronze medal and this is a chance of another medal right here.

1258
01:32:18,930 --> 01:32:24,534
Inward three and a half somersaults in the tuck position at 3.2 to post a score for a medal.

1259
01:32:29,931 --> 01:32:33,956
Oh no, and it's a miss, I'm afraid, from Ward.

1260
01:32:35,037 --> 01:32:40,944
I'll tell you what though, she might still go ahead of Marino.

1261
01:32:40,963 --> 01:32:48,853
A good tuck, just a little slow, hesitating coming out for that to kick over.

1262
01:32:52,457 --> 01:32:57,221
Everything's good at this point, but out too late, and kicks.

1263
01:32:58,653 --> 01:32:59,975
And 325.05.

1264
01:33:01,475 --> 01:33:05,320
She does get past Laura Murano of France to lead for the moment.

1265
01:33:08,363 --> 01:33:12,389
325 is still a good score.

1266
01:33:12,408 --> 01:33:14,971
Badkeet with her final dive.

1267
01:33:17,074 --> 01:33:24,323
She has not performed well this evening, but unbelievably, just down in fifth position, is there something for her?

1268
01:33:25,078 --> 01:33:26,980
still to be had from this competition.

1269
01:33:27,020 --> 01:33:29,824
3.2, the degree of difficulty for this back twister.

1270
01:33:30,444 --> 01:33:32,207
If she hits it, she can score big.

1271
01:33:37,554 --> 01:33:38,876
No.

1272
01:33:38,895 --> 01:33:40,978
And that's not going to do it.

1273
01:33:40,997 --> 01:33:46,385
No, she needed 74 points to go ahead of Georgia Wall to have any chance of a medal.

1274
01:33:46,904 --> 01:33:54,213
Doesn't get the jump, leans back, and very short.

1275
01:33:54,234 --> 01:33:55,034
Feet apart.

1276
01:33:55,657 --> 01:33:56,618
wobbling around.

1277
01:33:57,760 --> 01:33:59,141
That's a poor last eye for her.

1278
01:34:01,404 --> 01:34:03,266
You've got to get that jump up off the tower.

1279
01:34:04,288 --> 01:34:05,470
She just hasn't had that, has she?

1280
01:34:05,490 --> 01:34:07,092
She hasn't had that snap this evening.

1281
01:34:07,713 --> 01:34:10,537
3-0-8, 4-0, so third position at the moment.

1282
01:34:10,557 --> 01:34:18,948
Georgia Ward of Great Britain still leads on 325.05, with three or four challenges still in the mix.

1283
01:34:19,409 --> 01:34:23,975
And Constellation peck on the cheek there from Mum for Noemi Bakki.

1284
01:34:25,845 --> 01:34:28,310
Katerina Petrikova at sixth position.

1285
01:34:31,255 --> 01:34:36,181
Well, can she at least record a score to ask some questions here?

1286
01:34:38,166 --> 01:34:43,033
She would have to go nines to go ahead of Georgia Ward to get 81 points.

1287
01:34:45,757 --> 01:34:46,458
Oh, wow.

1288
01:34:46,479 --> 01:34:50,645
And is that back twister worth nines, Chris, on finals night?

1289
01:34:50,666 --> 01:34:51,766
It's not worth nines.

1290
01:34:52,569 --> 01:34:53,489
Maybe an eight.

1291
01:34:54,398 --> 01:34:57,841
The jump's good, very fast twist.

1292
01:34:57,862 --> 01:35:01,527
There's just too much splash to go any higher than an 8.

1293
01:35:02,828 --> 01:35:07,574
Technically good, but yeah, she doesn't get the final lockout.

1294
01:35:10,319 --> 01:35:11,140
Maybe 70s.

1295
01:35:11,640 --> 01:35:13,261
Well, judges agree with you.

1296
01:35:14,604 --> 01:35:18,529
Just the 1.8 in there, 7.5 for 72, 3.1605.

1297
01:35:20,051 --> 01:35:23,055
So Petrkova finishes up behind Georgia Ward.

1298
01:35:23,524 --> 01:35:28,911
And Ward moving ever closer to a medal.

1299
01:35:28,930 --> 01:35:34,976
Couriot, that one miss in the last round has basically cost her everything.

1300
01:35:37,238 --> 01:35:44,225
Back twister then, two and a half somersaults with one and a half twists in the pike position at 3.2, but she too would have to go near to the maximum.

1301
01:35:45,608 --> 01:35:52,755
Yeah, she would need nine and maybe one nine and a half to get to 3.25, which is what Georgia Ward's on.

1302
01:35:54,929 --> 01:35:59,194
No, doesn't get the jump, finishes below the board on that first one and a half twist.

1303
01:36:00,877 --> 01:36:06,846
Doesn't finish extending the legs on the jump, opening the pike, and ducks her head down on the entry.

1304
01:36:08,488 --> 01:36:12,775
And Ward has seen another challenger for a medal off.

1305
01:36:12,796 --> 01:36:21,408
And Courjou, who was one of the danger women in this draw, is below 300, and that's below par, way below par for her.

1306
01:36:23,313 --> 01:36:25,314
So Maria Curio signs off.

1307
01:36:26,655 --> 01:36:27,577
Three more to come.

1308
01:36:29,918 --> 01:36:34,783
And well, Wassen has got to find a phenomenal score.

1309
01:36:34,802 --> 01:36:36,765
And mathematically, it may not even be possible.

1310
01:36:36,805 --> 01:36:38,726
Well, nines, Chris Snow is saying.

1311
01:36:38,846 --> 01:36:44,152
Nines for Wassen if she wants to get close to Georgia Ward's score for a bronze medal.

1312
01:36:47,954 --> 01:36:48,836
It's a good dive.

1313
01:36:48,956 --> 01:36:50,157
It's a really good effort.

1314
01:36:50,237 --> 01:36:52,458
But again, it's not going to be enough.

1315
01:36:52,625 --> 01:36:58,914
No, that little movement on the end will keep it down to seven halves, maybe an eight again.

1316
01:36:59,836 --> 01:37:01,238
Just too much movement over.

1317
01:37:03,122 --> 01:37:10,113
She's watching on the replay, just bent legs a little bit, and I think she's gone over too far.

1318
01:37:10,132 --> 01:37:12,376
Well, you can hear those scores in the background.

1319
01:37:12,837 --> 01:37:18,024
You can multiply that against the 3.2, and what it means is that Georgia Ward

1320
01:37:18,561 --> 01:37:23,649
is going to take a medal away from this European Championship final.

1321
01:37:23,670 --> 01:37:26,895
The colour will be decided by the next two divers.

1322
01:37:26,975 --> 01:37:35,628
So Vasen signs off with 310 scored and Prokopchuk takes a big deep breath.

1323
01:37:35,930 --> 01:37:41,417
From her point of view, this back twister is all about shutting the door on the rest.

1324
01:37:42,740 --> 01:37:46,206
So to move into top spot, she doesn't have to do too much.

1325
01:37:50,894 --> 01:37:55,618
She just has to perform a fifth dive quite beautifully, and that's probably gold.

1326
01:37:55,859 --> 01:38:00,864
I tell you what, I reckon she's going to break the European record.

1327
01:38:01,045 --> 01:38:05,288
It's 373.3 that she set in 2013.

1328
01:38:05,328 --> 01:38:10,875
That is a really good call, Chris, and she thoroughly deserves it.

1329
01:38:10,895 --> 01:38:13,858
That's five rounds of cracking diving from Prokopchuk.

1330
01:38:14,519 --> 01:38:15,779
She's going to smash the record.

1331
01:38:15,800 --> 01:38:19,264
Certainly she's going to get more than 68 points.

1332
01:38:20,341 --> 01:38:28,753
And Prokopchuk looks like she's defended her title to make it five goals and a new European record at 385.90.

1333
01:38:30,155 --> 01:38:34,002
Prokopchuk reigning supreme here in this pool.

1334
01:38:34,222 --> 01:38:37,868
Now, that would have got her a bronze medal at the Olympic Games.

1335
01:38:37,967 --> 01:38:42,395
Well, that's what everybody's looking for against the rest of the world in Rio.

1336
01:38:42,555 --> 01:38:45,760
And Prokopchuk will go there in great form.

1337
01:38:46,862 --> 01:38:48,744
Couch then still diving for a medal.

1338
01:38:52,555 --> 01:38:53,617
And that'll do it.

1339
01:38:53,858 --> 01:38:59,992
Brilliant dive from Tonya Couch, and the celebration under the water tells you all you need to know.

1340
01:39:00,592 --> 01:39:01,314
She's done it.

1341
01:39:01,335 --> 01:39:03,498
She's got her medal at last.

1342
01:39:04,761 --> 01:39:06,024
And what a way to do it.

1343
01:39:06,864 --> 01:39:09,069
She's got tens on this dive before.

1344
01:39:09,832 --> 01:39:12,738
Not quite a ten because just a little splashy.

1345
01:39:13,421 --> 01:39:14,965
But look how high she finishes.

1346
01:39:15,024 --> 01:39:18,774
She just continues to float down from seven meters.

1347
01:39:19,595 --> 01:39:20,738
This is her favorite dive.

1348
01:39:20,779 --> 01:39:23,685
That's why she's got it here in round number five.

1349
01:39:23,725 --> 01:39:25,009
It's a reliable one.

1350
01:39:25,646 --> 01:39:29,090
We've promised you a good one to start the evening.

1351
01:39:29,551 --> 01:39:31,192
We've got a new European record.

1352
01:39:31,752 --> 01:39:34,215
We've got two medals for Great Britain.

1353
01:39:34,315 --> 01:39:39,581
Tonya Couch, at the expense of her compatriot, Georgia Ward, claims the silver.

1354
01:39:39,621 --> 01:39:43,984
But Georgia Ward will be delighted with her second medal at this Europeans.

1355
01:39:44,385 --> 01:39:46,507
But hats off to Lulia Prokopchuk.

1356
01:39:46,667 --> 01:39:52,092
That new record of 385.90 is right up there with the rest of the world.

1357
01:39:52,073 --> 01:39:59,213
and it's the defense of her title to make it five 10 meter gold medals for her and for Ukraine.

1358
01:39:59,314 --> 01:40:01,981
Brilliant performance, Prokopchuk is the champion.

